12
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:52,560
- Is everything in place? - You weren't supposed to relieve me.

13
00:00:52,810 --> 00:00:55,440
I know, but I felt like taking a shift.

14
00:00:55,980 --> 00:00:58,360
You like him, don't you? You like watching him.

15
00:00:58,610 --> 00:01:01,610
- Don't be ridiculous. - We're gonna kill him, you understand?

16
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:04,360
Morpheus believes he is the One.

17
00:01:04,610 --> 00:01:07,530
- Do you? - It doesn't matter what I believe.

18
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:09,410
You don't, do you?

19
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:11,740
- Did you hear that? - Hear what?

20
00:01:11,990 --> 00:01:13,580
Are you sure this line is clean?

21
00:01:13,830 --> 00:01:15,830
Yeah, of course I'm sure.

22
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:17,620
I better go.

23
00:01:55,580 --> 00:01:57,370
- Freeze! Police! - Hands on your head!

24
00:01:57,910 --> 00:01:59,000
Do it! Do it now!

25
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,730
Lieutenant.

26
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:23,020
Oh, shit.

27
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:27,070
Lieutenant, you were given specific orders.

28
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:29,030
I'm just doing my job.

29
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:32,330
You give me that "Juris-my-dick-tion" crap,

30
00:02:32,330 --> 00:02:34,080
you can cram it up your ass.

31
00:02:34,530 --> 00:02:37,040
The orders were for your protection.

32
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:40,750
I think we can handle one little girl.

33
00:02:45,880 --> 00:02:47,630
I sent two units!

34
00:02:47,880 --> 00:02:49,470
They're bringing her down now!

35
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:52,840
No, lieutenant, your men are already dead.

36
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:23,000
Shit.

37
00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:28,010
Morpheus, the line was traced. I don't know how.

38
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:29,840
I know, they cut the hard line.

39
00:03:30,090 --> 00:03:32,260
There's no time, you're gonna have to get to another exit.

40
00:03:32,510 --> 00:03:34,930
- Are there any agents? - Yes.

41
00:03:35,140 --> 00:03:36,310
Goddamn it.

42
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:38,100
You have to focus, Trinity.

43
00:03:38,350 --> 00:03:40,730
There's a phone at Wells and Lake,

44
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:42,770
you can make it.

45
00:03:43,020 --> 00:03:44,690
- All right. - Go,

46
00:04:46,830 --> 00:04:47,880
That's impossible.

47
00:05:22,870 --> 00:05:24,910
Get up, Trinity. Just get up.

48
00:05:25,540 --> 00:05:26,750
Get up.

49
00:06:12,630 --> 00:06:14,130
She got out.

50
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:15,710
It doesn't matter.

51
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:18,850
- The informant is real. - Yes

52
00:06:19,380 --> 00:06:21,050
We have the name of their next target.

53
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:22,970
The name is Neo.

54
00:06:26,270 --> 00:06:27,770
We'll need a search running.

55
00:06:28,060 --> 00:06:29,980
It has already begun.

64
00:07:24,550 --> 00:07:25,340
What?

65
00:07:31,710 --> 00:07:33,210
What the hell?

68
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:42,800
"Follow the white rabbit."

70
00:07:54,650 --> 00:07:55,810
Who is it?

71
00:07:56,060 --> 00:07:57,360
It's Choi.

72
00:08:10,870 --> 00:08:12,040
You're two hours late.

73
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:14,370
I know. It's her fault.

74
00:08:14,670 --> 00:08:16,710
You got the money?

75
00:08:17,750 --> 00:08:18,920
Two grand.

76
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:20,920
Hold on.

77
00:08:38,610 --> 00:08:39,980
Hallelujah.

78
00:08:40,230 --> 00:08:43,110
You're my savior, man. My own personal Jesus Christ.

79
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:45,240
You get caught using that...

80
00:08:45,490 --> 00:08:47,620
I know. This never happened. You don't exist.

81
00:08:48,740 --> 00:08:50,830
- Right. - Something wrong, man?

82
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:53,120
You look a little whiter than usual.

83
00:08:54,250 --> 00:08:56,420
My computer, it...

84
00:08:59,420 --> 00:09:01,190
Ever have that feeling where

85
00:09:01,190 --> 00:09:03,970
you're not sure if you're awake or still dreaming?

86
00:09:04,760 --> 00:09:07,510
All the time. It's called mescaline.

87
00:09:08,010 --> 00:09:10,140
It's the only way to fly.

88
00:09:11,010 --> 00:09:13,520
It just sounds to me like now you need to unplug, man.

89
00:09:14,270 --> 00:09:16,310
Get some R and R?

90
00:09:16,690 --> 00:09:20,440
What do you think, Dujour? Should we take him with us?

91
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:23,650
Definitely.

92
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:27,030
No, I can't. I have work tomorrow.

93
00:09:27,570 --> 00:09:28,700
Come on.

94
00:09:28,950 --> 00:09:31,580
It'll be fun. I promise.

95
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:39,590
Yeah.

96
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:42,300
Sure. I'll go.

97
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:10,950
Hello, Neo.

98
00:10:12,490 --> 00:10:16,000
- How do you know that name? - I know a lot about you.

99
00:10:16,870 --> 00:10:18,960
- Who are you? - My name is Trinity.

100
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:21,130
Trinity.

101
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:26,090
The Trinity? That cracked the IRS D-base?

102
00:10:26,340 --> 00:10:27,800
That was a long time ago.

103
00:10:28,050 --> 00:10:29,970
- Jesus. - What?

104
00:10:30,430 --> 00:10:32,220
I just thought...

105
00:10:33,970 --> 00:10:35,140
you were a guy.

106
00:10:35,390 --> 00:10:36,850
Most guys do.

107
00:10:38,060 --> 00:10:40,270
That was you on my computer.

108
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:42,020
How did you do that?

109
00:10:42,650 --> 00:10:45,360
Right now, all I can tell you...

110
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:47,530
...is that you're in danger.

111
00:10:47,990 --> 00:10:50,410
- I brought you here to warn you. - Of what?

112
00:10:50,990 --> 00:10:52,660
They're watching you, Neo.

113
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:55,660
- Who is? - Please just listen.

114
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:01,000
I know why you're here, Neo.

115
00:11:01,790 --> 00:11:03,750
I know what you've been doing.

116
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,880
I know why you hardly sleep...

117
00:11:06,170 --> 00:11:09,300
why you live alone and why, night after night...

118
00:11:09,550 --> 00:11:11,890
you sit at your computer.

119
00:11:13,050 --> 00:11:14,600
You're looking for him.

120
00:11:15,390 --> 00:11:18,390
I know, because I was once looking for the same thing.

121
00:11:18,890 --> 00:11:21,020
And when he found me...

122
00:11:21,650 --> 00:11:24,730
he told me I wasn't really looking for him...

123
00:11:25,650 --> 00:11:27,400
I was looking for an answer.

124
00:11:28,030 --> 00:11:31,150
It's the question that drives us, Neo.

125
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:34,490
It's the question that brought you here.

126
00:11:36,580 --> 00:11:37,950
You know the question...

127
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,710
just as I did.

128
00:11:41,250 --> 00:11:42,870
What is the Matrix?

129
00:11:43,130 --> 00:11:45,590
The answer is out there, Neo.

130
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:48,260
It's looking for you.

131
00:11:49,050 --> 00:11:50,760
And it will find you...

132
00:11:51,010 --> 00:11:53,010
if you want it to.

133
00:11:59,810 --> 00:12:00,850
Shit.

134
00:12:01,020 --> 00:12:02,140
Shit, shit.

135
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:15,240
You have a problem with authority, Mr. Anderson.

136
00:12:15,490 --> 00:12:17,450
You believe that you are special,

137
00:12:17,450 --> 00:12:19,540
that somehow the rules do not apply to you.

138
00:12:20,250 --> 00:12:22,250
Obviously, you are mistaken.

139
00:12:25,210 --> 00:12:28,090
This company is one of the top software companies in the world...

140
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:31,720
because every single employee understands they are part of a whole.

141
00:12:31,970 --> 00:12:36,600
Thus, if an employee has a problem, the company has a problem.

142
00:12:38,850 --> 00:12:42,060
The time has come to make a choice, Mr. Anderson.

143
00:12:42,940 --> 00:12:44,290
Either you choose to be

144
00:12:44,290 --> 00:12:46,810
at your desk on time from this day forth...

145
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:50,030
or you choose to find yourself another job.

146
00:12:50,900 --> 00:12:52,240
Do I make myself clear?

147
00:12:52,490 --> 00:12:54,910
Yes, Mr. Rhineheart. Perfectly clear.

148
00:13:03,370 --> 00:13:05,370
Thomas Anderson?

149
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:07,920
Yeah, that's me.

150
00:13:15,930 --> 00:13:17,090
Great.

151
00:13:18,510 --> 00:13:19,680
Have a nice day.

152
00:13:35,490 --> 00:13:39,830
- Hello? - Hello, Neo, Do you know who this is?

153
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:43,830
- Morpheus. - Yes.

154
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:46,080
I've been looking for you.

155
00:13:46,330 --> 00:13:49,500
I don't know if you're ready to see what I want to show you.

156
00:13:49,750 --> 00:13:52,920
But unfortunately, you and I have run out of time,

157
00:13:53,170 --> 00:13:54,480
They're coming for you, Neo,

158
00:13:54,490 --> 00:13:56,880
and I don't know what they're going to do,

159
00:13:57,130 --> 00:13:58,470
Who's coming for me?

160
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:00,800
Stand up and see for yourself.

161
00:14:01,050 --> 00:14:05,350
- What? Right now? - Yes, now.

162
00:14:06,230 --> 00:14:08,100
Do it slowly.

163
00:14:08,520 --> 00:14:09,730
The elevator.

164
00:14:14,610 --> 00:14:16,600
- Oh, shit! - Yes.

165
00:14:21,070 --> 00:14:22,200
What the hell do they want from me?

166
00:14:22,370 --> 00:14:24,390
I don't know, but if you don't want to find out,

167
00:14:24,390 --> 00:14:25,790
I suggest you get out of there.

168
00:14:25,950 --> 00:14:27,000
How?

169
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:30,250
I can guide you, but you must do exactly as I say.

170
00:14:30,510 --> 00:14:30,990
Okay.

171
00:14:31,130 --> 00:14:33,130
The cubicle across from you is empty.

172
00:14:36,260 --> 00:14:38,380
- But what if they... - Go, Now.

173
00:14:45,140 --> 00:14:47,520
Stay here for just a moment.

174
00:14:54,730 --> 00:14:57,490
When I tell you, go to the end of the row...

175
00:14:57,740 --> 00:14:59,700
to the office at the end of the hall.

176
00:14:59,950 --> 00:15:02,320
Stay as low as you can.

177
00:15:04,700 --> 00:15:05,740
Go! Now!

178
00:15:20,130 --> 00:15:23,680
Good, now, outside there is a scaffold.

179
00:15:26,390 --> 00:15:28,730
- How do you know all this? - We don't have time, Neo.

180
00:15:28,980 --> 00:15:31,810
To your left there's a window, go to it.

181
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:35,610
Open it.

182
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:38,240
You can use the scaffold to get to the roof,

183
00:15:38,490 --> 00:15:41,070
No way! No way! This is crazy!

184
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:43,700
There are two ways out of this building.

185
00:15:43,950 --> 00:15:47,740
One is that scaffold, the other is in their custody.

186
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:51,210
You take a chance either way, I leave it to you.

187
00:15:54,790 --> 00:15:56,550
This is insane!

188
00:15:57,710 --> 00:15:59,590
Why is this happening to me?

189
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:01,510
What'd I do?

190
00:16:01,880 --> 00:16:04,640
I'm nobody. I didn't do anything.

191
00:16:05,220 --> 00:16:06,680
I'm gonna die.

192
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:17,520
Shit!

193
00:16:37,790 --> 00:16:38,920
Oh, shit!

194
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:45,680
I can't do this.

195
00:16:58,270 --> 00:16:59,360
Shit.

196
00:17:48,620 --> 00:17:50,290
As you can see, we've had

197
00:17:50,300 --> 00:17:53,450
our eye on you for some time now, Mr. Anderson.

198
00:17:54,750 --> 00:17:57,420
It seems that you've been living...

199
00:17:57,670 --> 00:17:59,790
two lives.

200
00:18:01,210 --> 00:18:03,710
In one life, you're Thomas A. Anderson...

201
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:07,300
program writer for a respectable software company.

202
00:18:08,340 --> 00:18:11,640
You have a social security number. You pay your taxes.

203
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:13,350
And you...

204
00:18:14,930 --> 00:18:18,560
help your landlady carry out her garbage.

205
00:18:21,060 --> 00:18:24,190
The other life is lived in computers...

206
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:27,450
where you go by the hacker alias "Neo"...

207
00:18:27,700 --> 00:18:29,780
and are guilty of virtually

208
00:18:29,780 --> 00:18:32,490
every computer crime we have a law for.

209
00:18:33,790 --> 00:18:35,750
One of these lives...

210
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,830
has a future.

211
00:18:38,170 --> 00:18:40,170
And one of them does not.

212
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:47,720
I'm going to be as forthcoming as I can be, Mr. Anderson.

213
00:18:48,720 --> 00:18:50,050
You're here...

214
00:18:50,390 --> 00:18:52,640
because we need your help.

215
00:18:56,270 --> 00:18:59,270
We know that you've been contacted by a certain...

216
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:01,310
individual.

217
00:19:02,230 --> 00:19:06,280
A man who calls himself "Morpheus".

218
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:11,280
Whatever you think you know about this man is irrelevant.

219
00:19:11,530 --> 00:19:13,950
He is considered by many authorities...

220
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:17,250
to be the most dangerous man alive.

221
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,210
My colleagues...

222
00:19:21,630 --> 00:19:24,540
believe that I am wasting my time with you.

223
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:28,260
But I believe you wish to do the right thing.

224
00:19:28,550 --> 00:19:32,050
We're willing to wipe the slate clean...

225
00:19:32,430 --> 00:19:34,550
give you a fresh start.

226
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:37,980
All we're asking in return is your cooperation...

227
00:19:38,230 --> 00:19:41,730
in bringing a known terrorist to justice.

228
00:19:43,110 --> 00:19:44,360
Yeah.

229
00:19:45,650 --> 00:19:47,730
That sounds like a really good deal.

230
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:51,110
But I think I got a better one.

231
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:52,860
How about...

232
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:55,280
I give you the finger...

233
00:19:57,870 --> 00:19:59,910
and you give me my phone call.

234
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:03,920
Mr. Anderson...

235
00:20:07,880 --> 00:20:09,130
you disappoint me.

236
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:12,010
You can't scare me with this gestapo crap.

237
00:20:12,260 --> 00:20:13,640
I know my rights.

238
00:20:13,890 --> 00:20:15,390
I want my phone call.

239
00:20:15,970 --> 00:20:18,140
Tell me, Mr. Anderson...

240
00:20:19,020 --> 00:20:20,430
what good is a phone call...

241
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:24,270
if you're unable to speak?

242
00:20:58,060 --> 00:21:00,270
You're going to help us, Mr. Anderson...

243
00:21:00,970 --> 00:21:03,060
whether you want to or not.

244
00:22:01,370 --> 00:22:04,620
This line is tapped, so I must be brief.

245
00:22:04,870 --> 00:22:06,200
They got to you first,

246
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:09,170
but they've underestimated how important you are.

247
00:22:09,420 --> 00:22:11,250
If they knew what I know...

248
00:22:11,500 --> 00:22:13,510
you would probably be dead.

249
00:22:14,510 --> 00:22:18,220
What are you talking about? What is happening to me?

250
00:22:18,470 --> 00:22:23,310
You are the One, Neo. You see, you may have spent the last few years...

251
00:22:23,560 --> 00:22:26,520
looking for me, but I've spent my entire life...

252
00:22:26,770 --> 00:22:28,270
looking for you.

253
00:22:29,810 --> 00:22:31,980
Now, do you still want to meet?

254
00:22:32,940 --> 00:22:35,820
- Yes. - Then go to the Adams Street bridge.

255
00:22:46,040 --> 00:22:47,250
Get in.

256
00:22:59,510 --> 00:23:01,540
- What the hell is this? - It's necessary, Neo.

257
00:23:02,410 --> 00:23:03,140
For our protection.

258
00:23:03,390 --> 00:23:05,560
- From what? - From you.

259
00:23:07,100 --> 00:23:08,560
- Take off your shirt. - What?

260
00:23:08,890 --> 00:23:10,850
Stop the car.

261
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:15,650
Listen, coppertop.

262
00:23:15,900 --> 00:23:17,900
We don't have time for 20 Questions.

263
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:20,780
Right now, there's only one rule:

264
00:23:21,070 --> 00:23:22,410
Our way...

265
00:23:22,740 --> 00:23:23,830
or the highway.

266
00:23:30,330 --> 00:23:31,460
Fine.

267
00:23:33,340 --> 00:23:35,800
Please, Neo, you have to trust me.

268
00:23:36,380 --> 00:23:39,010
- Why? - Because you have been down there, Neo.

269
00:23:39,760 --> 00:23:40,970
You know that road.

270
00:23:41,970 --> 00:23:43,640
You know exactly where it ends.

271
00:23:45,810 --> 00:23:48,060
And I know that's not where you want to be.

272
00:24:02,240 --> 00:24:03,780
Apoc, lights.

273
00:24:06,290 --> 00:24:08,450
Lie back. Lift up your shirt.

274
00:24:10,370 --> 00:24:12,620
- What's that? - We think you're bugged.

275
00:24:20,380 --> 00:24:21,840
Try and relax.

276
00:24:28,140 --> 00:24:29,310
Come on.

277
00:24:30,520 --> 00:24:32,560
Come on.

278
00:24:33,190 --> 00:24:35,230
It's on the move.

279
00:24:35,940 --> 00:24:37,150
Come on, you shit.

280
00:24:38,980 --> 00:24:41,070
- You're gonna lose it. - No, I'm not.

281
00:24:41,240 --> 00:24:42,490
Clear!

282
00:24:51,080 --> 00:24:53,210
Jesus Christ! That thing's real?!

283
00:25:26,950 --> 00:25:28,280
This is it.

284
00:25:31,620 --> 00:25:34,080
Let me give you one piece of advice.

285
00:25:35,040 --> 00:25:36,710
Be honest.

286
00:25:38,290 --> 00:25:40,500
He knows more than you can imagine.

287
00:25:49,220 --> 00:25:50,560
At last.

288
00:25:52,100 --> 00:25:53,180
Welcome, Neo.

289
00:25:54,390 --> 00:25:56,310
As you no doubt have guessed...

290
00:25:56,560 --> 00:25:57,810
I am Morpheus.

291
00:25:58,860 --> 00:26:00,440
It's an honor to meet you.

292
00:26:00,900 --> 00:26:01,940
No...

293
00:26:02,530 --> 00:26:03,820
the honor is mine.

294
00:26:04,740 --> 00:26:07,240
Please, come. Sit.

295
00:26:22,340 --> 00:26:23,960
I imagine...

296
00:26:24,380 --> 00:26:27,130
that right now you're feeling a bit like Alice,

297
00:26:28,840 --> 00:26:31,260
tumbling down the rabbit hole?

298
00:26:32,180 --> 00:26:33,930
You could say that.

299
00:26:34,100 --> 00:26:36,730
I can see it in your eyes.

300
00:26:37,310 --> 00:26:40,610
You have the look of a man who accepts what he sees,

301
00:26:40,860 --> 00:26:43,110
because he's expecting to wake up.

302
00:26:44,530 --> 00:26:47,150
Ironically, this is not far from the truth.

303
00:26:47,820 --> 00:26:50,320
Do you believe in fate, Neo?

304
00:26:50,620 --> 00:26:52,910
- No. - Why not?

305
00:26:53,160 --> 00:26:55,950
Because I don't like the idea that I'm not in control of my life.

306
00:26:57,040 --> 00:27:00,380
I know exactly what you mean.

307
00:27:04,670 --> 00:27:07,050
Let me tell you why you're here.

308
00:27:08,090 --> 00:27:09,640
You're here brecause you know something.

309
00:27:10,180 --> 00:27:11,800
What you know, you can't explain.

310
00:27:12,300 --> 00:27:13,890
But you feel it.

311
00:27:14,470 --> 00:27:16,390
You felt it your entire life.

312
00:27:16,980 --> 00:27:18,970
That there's something wrong with the world.

313
00:27:18,970 --> 00:27:21,150
You don't know what it is, but it's there.

314
00:27:21,650 --> 00:27:23,860
Like a splinter in your mind,

315
00:27:24,110 --> 00:27:25,980
driving you mad.

316
00:27:26,900 --> 00:27:29,660
It is this feeling that has brought you to me.

317
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:34,030
Do you know what I'm talking about?

318
00:27:35,870 --> 00:27:37,200
The Matrix?

319
00:27:39,710 --> 00:27:41,380
Do you want to know

320
00:27:41,830 --> 00:27:43,840
what it is?

321
00:27:46,210 --> 00:27:48,090
The Matrix is everywhere.

322
00:27:48,340 --> 00:27:50,050
It is all around us.

323
00:27:50,300 --> 00:27:52,260
Even now, in this very room.

324
00:27:53,100 --> 00:27:55,310
You can see it when you look out your window,

325
00:27:55,560 --> 00:27:57,890
or when you turn on your television.

326
00:27:58,310 --> 00:28:00,850
You can feel it when you go to work,

327
00:28:02,400 --> 00:28:04,060
when you go to church,

328
00:28:04,480 --> 00:28:06,570
when you pay your taxes.

329
00:28:07,690 --> 00:28:10,610
It is the world that has been pulled over your eyes

330
00:28:10,860 --> 00:28:12,450
to blind you from the truth.

331
00:28:14,660 --> 00:28:15,910
What truth?

332
00:28:20,160 --> 00:28:21,710
That you are a slave, Neo.

333
00:28:23,210 --> 00:28:25,500
Like everyone else, you were born into bondage,

334
00:28:25,750 --> 00:28:30,420
born into a prison that you cannot smell or taste or touch.

335
00:28:30,720 --> 00:28:33,430
A prison for your mind.

336
00:28:40,390 --> 00:28:42,730
Unfortunately, no one can be...

337
00:28:43,060 --> 00:28:45,440
told what the Matrix is.

338
00:28:48,900 --> 00:28:50,780
You have to see it for yourself.

339
00:29:00,290 --> 00:29:02,580
This is your last chance.

340
00:29:02,830 --> 00:29:05,170
After this, there is no turning back.

341
00:29:05,630 --> 00:29:07,130
You take the blue pill,

342
00:29:07,420 --> 00:29:10,710
the story ends, you wake up in your bed and believe

343
00:29:10,710 --> 00:29:12,510
whatever you want to believe.

344
00:29:12,760 --> 00:29:14,090
You take the red pill,

345
00:29:14,340 --> 00:29:16,300
you stay in Wonderland,

346
00:29:16,800 --> 00:29:19,510
and I show you how deep the rabbit hole goes.

347
00:29:29,400 --> 00:29:30,610
Remember,

348
00:29:31,440 --> 00:29:34,490
all I'm offering is the truth. Nothing more.

349
00:29:48,790 --> 00:29:50,130
Follow me.

350
00:29:52,670 --> 00:29:54,340
Apoc, are we on-line?

351
00:29:54,590 --> 00:29:55,970
Almost.

352
00:29:59,300 --> 00:30:01,350
Time is always against us.

353
00:30:01,720 --> 00:30:03,230
Please take a seat there.

354
00:30:21,410 --> 00:30:23,120
You did all this?

355
00:30:27,250 --> 00:30:29,250
The pill you took is part of a trace program.

356
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:32,750
It's designed to disrupt your input/outout carrier signals

357
00:30:32,750 --> 00:30:34,630
so we can pinpoint your location.

358
00:30:35,170 --> 00:30:36,220
What does that mean?

359
00:30:36,800 --> 00:30:38,970
It means buckle your seat belt, Dorothy,

360
00:30:39,300 --> 00:30:40,640
because Kansas

361
00:30:40,890 --> 00:30:41,930
is going bye-bye.

362
00:31:19,840 --> 00:31:21,220
Did you...

363
00:31:32,230 --> 00:31:34,270
Have you ever had a dream, Neo,

364
00:31:34,280 --> 00:31:36,320
that you were so sure was real?

365
00:31:37,780 --> 00:31:40,360
What if you were unable to wake from that dream?

366
00:31:40,610 --> 00:31:43,120
How would you know the difference between the dream world

367
00:31:43,740 --> 00:31:45,160
and the real world?

368
00:31:46,790 --> 00:31:49,160
- This can't be. - Be what?

369
00:31:49,870 --> 00:31:51,380
Be real?

370
00:31:55,340 --> 00:31:56,290
It's going into replication.

371
00:31:56,470 --> 00:31:58,420
- Apoc? - Still nothing.

372
00:31:58,420 --> 00:31:59,760
It's cold.

373
00:32:00,010 --> 00:32:01,390
It's cold!

374
00:32:05,260 --> 00:32:06,930
Tank, we're going to need a signal soon.

375
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:11,100
- I got a fibrillation. - Apoc, location.

376
00:32:11,350 --> 00:32:12,810
Targeting almost there.

377
00:32:16,110 --> 00:32:17,530
He's going into arrest.

378
00:32:17,780 --> 00:32:20,280
- Lock. I got him! - Now, Tank, now!

379
00:35:17,540 --> 00:35:18,620
Welcome

380
00:35:18,960 --> 00:35:20,880
to the real world.

381
00:35:22,290 --> 00:35:24,130
We've done it, Trinity.

382
00:35:24,380 --> 00:35:25,920
We found him.

383
00:35:26,170 --> 00:35:28,970
- I hope you're right. - I don't have to hope.

384
00:35:29,550 --> 00:35:31,140
I know it.

385
00:35:36,310 --> 00:35:37,350
Am I dead?

386
00:35:37,850 --> 00:35:40,020
Far from it.

387
00:35:53,990 --> 00:35:55,410
He still needs a lot of work.

388
00:35:56,950 --> 00:35:58,040
What are you doing?

389
00:35:58,290 --> 00:36:00,500
Your muscles have atrophied. We're rebuilding them.

390
00:36:01,080 --> 00:36:02,630
Why do my eyes hurt?

391
00:36:03,340 --> 00:36:05,210
You've never used them before.

392
00:36:09,170 --> 00:36:11,930
Rest, Neo. The answers are coming.

393
00:37:26,500 --> 00:37:28,090
Morpheus, what's happened to me?

394
00:37:28,840 --> 00:37:30,250
What is this place?

395
00:37:30,250 --> 00:37:32,720
More important than "what" is "when."

396
00:37:33,430 --> 00:37:36,510
- When? - You believe it's the year 1999,

397
00:37:36,760 --> 00:37:39,010
when in fact, it's closer to 2199.

398
00:37:40,140 --> 00:37:42,890
I can't tell you exactly what year it is,

399
00:37:43,140 --> 00:37:44,770
because we honestly don't know.

400
00:37:45,270 --> 00:37:48,110
There's nothing I can say that will explain it for you, Neo.

401
00:37:48,360 --> 00:37:49,520
Come with me.

402
00:37:49,820 --> 00:37:51,110
See for yourself.

403
00:37:51,650 --> 00:37:53,400
This is my ship.

404
00:37:53,700 --> 00:37:56,620
The Nebuchadnezzar, It's a hovercraft.

405
00:37:59,450 --> 00:38:01,200
This is the main deck.

406
00:38:07,040 --> 00:38:08,210
This is the core,

408
00:38:10,710 --> 00:38:14,470
where we broadcast our pirate signal and hack into the Matrix.

409
00:38:17,840 --> 00:38:21,010
Most of my crew you already know.

410
00:38:26,020 --> 00:38:27,440
This is Apoc,

411
00:38:28,230 --> 00:38:29,560
Switch,

412
00:38:31,150 --> 00:38:32,320
and Cypher.

413
00:38:32,570 --> 00:38:36,280
The ones you don't know: Tank and his big brother, Dozer.

414
00:38:37,160 --> 00:38:39,580
The little one behind you is Mouse.

415
00:38:43,910 --> 00:38:47,170
You wanted to know what the Matrix is, Neo?

416
00:38:48,210 --> 00:38:49,420
Trinity.

417
00:39:10,440 --> 00:39:12,020
Try to relax.

418
00:39:16,900 --> 00:39:18,740
This will feel a little weird.

419
00:39:30,710 --> 00:39:31,880
This

420
00:39:32,250 --> 00:39:33,960
is the Construct.

421
00:39:34,380 --> 00:39:36,510
It's our loading program.

422
00:39:36,760 --> 00:39:39,220
We can load anything, from clothing,

423
00:39:39,470 --> 00:39:40,840
to equipment,

424
00:39:41,140 --> 00:39:42,470
weapons,

425
00:39:43,100 --> 00:39:44,930
training simulations,

426
00:39:45,310 --> 00:39:47,850
anything we need.

427
00:39:50,650 --> 00:39:53,070
Right now we're inside a computer program?

428
00:39:53,360 --> 00:39:55,280
Is it really so hard to believe?

429
00:39:55,780 --> 00:39:56,860
Your clothes are different.

430
00:39:56,860 --> 00:39:58,400
The plugs in your arms and head are gone.

431
00:39:59,610 --> 00:40:01,700
Your hair has changed.

432
00:40:02,070 --> 00:40:05,410
Your appearance now is what we call "residual self-image."

433
00:40:06,120 --> 00:40:08,750
It is the mental projection of your digital self.

434
00:40:14,630 --> 00:40:15,750
This isn't real?

435
00:40:16,000 --> 00:40:17,550
What is "real"?

436
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:20,180
How do you define "real"?

437
00:40:20,470 --> 00:40:22,390
If you're talking about what you can feel,

438
00:40:22,640 --> 00:40:25,060
what you can smell, taste and see,

439
00:40:25,310 --> 00:40:26,650
then "real" is simply

440
00:40:26,660 --> 00:40:29,180
electrical signals interpreted by your brain.

441
00:40:33,360 --> 00:40:35,770
This is the world that you know.

442
00:40:37,190 --> 00:40:40,240
The world as it was at the end of the 20th century.

443
00:40:42,610 --> 00:40:46,950
It exists now only as part of a neural-interactive simulation

444
00:40:47,200 --> 00:40:48,450
that we call the Matrix.

445
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:55,840
You've been living in a dream world, Neo.

446
00:40:56,800 --> 00:40:57,920
This is the world

447
00:40:58,210 --> 00:41:00,010
as it exists today.

448
00:41:13,020 --> 00:41:15,980
Welcome to "the desert

449
00:41:16,860 --> 00:41:18,440
of the real."

450
00:41:21,820 --> 00:41:24,200
We have only bits and pieces of information.

451
00:41:24,450 --> 00:41:25,970
But what we know for certain

452
00:41:25,970 --> 00:41:28,240
is that at some point in the early 21st century,

453
00:41:28,490 --> 00:41:31,750
all of mankind was united in celebration.

454
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:34,680
We marveled at our own magnificence

455
00:41:34,680 --> 00:41:37,250
as we gave birth to A.I.

456
00:41:37,540 --> 00:41:38,670
AI
A.I.

457
00:41:39,710 --> 00:41:41,090
You mean artificial intelligence.

458
00:41:41,340 --> 00:41:43,110
A singular consciousness

459
00:41:43,110 --> 00:41:45,760
that spawned an entire race of machines.

460
00:41:46,600 --> 00:41:50,060
We don't know who struck first, us or them.

461
00:41:50,470 --> 00:41:53,690
But we know that it was us that scorched the sky.

462
00:41:55,350 --> 00:41:57,520
At the time, they were dependent on solar power,

463
00:41:57,770 --> 00:42:01,110
and it was believed that they would be unable to survive

464
00:42:01,440 --> 00:42:04,950
without an energy source as abundant as the sun.

465
00:42:05,200 --> 00:42:06,920
Throughout human history,

466
00:42:06,920 --> 00:42:10,080
we have been dependent on machines to survive.

467
00:42:11,540 --> 00:42:15,750
Fate, it seems, is not without a sense of irony.

468
00:42:18,960 --> 00:42:20,520
The human body generates

469
00:42:20,520 --> 00:42:23,380
more bioelectricity than a 120-volt battery.

470
00:42:23,630 --> 00:42:27,760
And over 25,000 BTUs of body heat.

471
00:42:29,680 --> 00:42:31,850
Combined with a form of fusion,

472
00:42:32,180 --> 00:42:37,020
the machines had found all the energy they would ever need.

473
00:42:41,070 --> 00:42:44,820
There are fields, Neo, endless fields,

474
00:42:45,070 --> 00:42:48,320
where human beings are no longer born.

475
00:42:49,030 --> 00:42:50,870
We are grown.

476
00:42:56,920 --> 00:42:59,500
For the longest time, I wouldn't believe it.

477
00:42:59,750 --> 00:43:02,420
And then I saw the fields with my own eyes,

478
00:43:03,760 --> 00:43:05,380
watched them liquefy the dead

479
00:43:05,630 --> 00:43:08,970
so they could be fed intravenously to the living.

480
00:43:09,510 --> 00:43:13,770
And standing there, facing the pure, horrifying precision,

481
00:43:14,020 --> 00:43:16,940
I came to realize the obviousness of the truth.

482
00:43:19,560 --> 00:43:21,360
What is the Matrix?

483
00:43:22,570 --> 00:43:23,610
Control.

484
00:43:24,990 --> 00:43:28,360
The Matrix is a computer-generated dream world,

485
00:43:29,160 --> 00:43:32,240
built to keep us under control,

486
00:43:33,410 --> 00:43:36,580
in order to change a human being

487
00:43:37,210 --> 00:43:38,370
into this.

488
00:43:39,750 --> 00:43:40,880
No.

489
00:43:42,500 --> 00:43:44,090
I don't believe it.

490
00:43:44,460 --> 00:43:45,670
It's not possible.

491
00:43:46,260 --> 00:43:48,250
I didn't say it would be easy, Neo.

492
00:43:48,250 --> 00:43:50,840
I just said it would be the truth.

493
00:43:51,090 --> 00:43:52,680
Stop!

494
00:43:52,930 --> 00:43:54,140
Let me out!

495
00:43:54,850 --> 00:43:56,770
Let me out! I want out!

496
00:43:58,730 --> 00:44:01,400
- Easy, Neo. Easy. - Get this thing out of me.

497
00:44:01,650 --> 00:44:03,320
Get this thing out of me!

498
00:44:05,110 --> 00:44:06,610
Don't touch me!

499
00:44:06,860 --> 00:44:08,490
Stay away from me!

500
00:44:08,900 --> 00:44:10,410
I don't believe it.

501
00:44:11,110 --> 00:44:12,320
I don't believe it.

502
00:44:12,570 --> 00:44:14,160
I don't believe it.

503
00:44:14,330 --> 00:44:17,830
- He's gonna pop. - Breathe, Neo. Just breathe.

504
00:44:36,220 --> 00:44:38,020
I can't go back, can I?

505
00:44:38,600 --> 00:44:39,940
No.

506
00:44:41,100 --> 00:44:42,310
But if you could,

507
00:44:43,150 --> 00:44:44,650
would you really want to?

508
00:44:47,150 --> 00:44:48,570
I feel I owe you an apology.

509
00:44:49,110 --> 00:44:50,490
We have a rule.

510
00:44:50,950 --> 00:44:54,320
We never free a mind once it's reached a certain age.

511
00:44:54,580 --> 00:44:57,870
It's dangerous. The mind has trouble letting go.

512
00:44:58,120 --> 00:45:00,410
I've seen it before, and I'm sorry.

513
00:45:01,460 --> 00:45:03,540
I did what I did because...

514
00:45:04,250 --> 00:45:05,710
I had to.

515
00:45:14,140 --> 00:45:18,220
When the Matrix was first built, there was a man born inside,

516
00:45:18,720 --> 00:45:22,520
who had the ability to change whatever he wanted,

517
00:45:22,890 --> 00:45:25,810
to remake the Matrix as he saw fit.

518
00:45:27,570 --> 00:45:31,030
It was he who freed the first of us,

519
00:45:31,900 --> 00:45:33,530
taught us the truth.

520
00:45:34,990 --> 00:45:38,080
As long as the Matrix exists,

521
00:45:38,410 --> 00:45:40,500
the human race will never be free.

522
00:45:44,710 --> 00:45:46,250
After he died,

523
00:45:47,000 --> 00:45:49,710
the Oracle prophesied his return,

524
00:45:50,260 --> 00:45:51,340
and that his coming

525
00:45:51,340 --> 00:45:53,470
would hail the destruction of the Matrix,

526
00:45:53,720 --> 00:45:55,390
end the war,

527
00:45:55,720 --> 00:45:56,930
bring freedom to our people.

528
00:45:58,310 --> 00:45:59,950
That is why there are those

529
00:45:59,950 --> 00:46:02,940
of us who spent our lives searching the Matrix,

530
00:46:03,270 --> 00:46:04,850
looking for him.

531
00:46:07,270 --> 00:46:09,360
I did what I did because...

532
00:46:10,980 --> 00:46:13,110
I believe that search is over.

533
00:46:18,200 --> 00:46:19,620
Get some rest.

534
00:46:20,240 --> 00:46:22,040
You're going to need it.

535
00:46:24,790 --> 00:46:26,750
For what?

536
00:46:28,880 --> 00:46:30,050
Your training.

537
00:46:48,360 --> 00:46:50,070
Morning. Did you sleep?

538
00:46:50,940 --> 00:46:52,150
You will tonight.

539
00:46:52,530 --> 00:46:54,070
I guarantee it.

540
00:46:55,570 --> 00:46:57,490
I'm Tank. I'll be your operator.

541
00:46:57,950 --> 00:47:00,370
- You don't have any... - Holes? Nope.

542
00:47:01,290 --> 00:47:03,540
Me and my brother, Dozer, are 100%

543
00:47:03,540 --> 00:47:06,000
pure, old-fashioned, homegrown human.

544
00:47:06,250 --> 00:47:07,460
Born free right here,

545
00:47:08,000 --> 00:47:09,330
in the real world.

546
00:47:09,590 --> 00:47:11,250
Genuine child of Zion.

547
00:47:12,090 --> 00:47:14,550
- Zion? - If the war was over tomorrow,

548
00:47:14,800 --> 00:47:16,220
Zion's where the party would be.

549
00:47:16,720 --> 00:47:18,010
It's a city?

550
00:47:18,260 --> 00:47:21,430
The last human city. The only place we have left.

551
00:47:23,020 --> 00:47:24,270
Where is it?

552
00:47:25,640 --> 00:47:27,020
Deep underground,

553
00:47:27,270 --> 00:47:29,440
near the Earth's core, where it's still warm.

554
00:47:31,060 --> 00:47:32,940
You live long enough, you might see it.

555
00:47:35,190 --> 00:47:37,990
Goddamn! I gotta tell you,

556
00:47:37,990 --> 00:47:40,030
I feel the excited to see what you're capable of

557
00:47:40,280 --> 00:47:42,030
if Morpheus is right and all.

558
00:47:42,530 --> 00:47:45,290
We're not supposed to talk about this, but...

559
00:47:45,540 --> 00:47:46,960
if you are,

560
00:47:48,040 --> 00:47:50,040
it's a very exciting time.

561
00:47:51,080 --> 00:47:53,800
We got a lot to do. We gotta get to it.

562
00:47:57,720 --> 00:48:00,640
We're supposed to start with these operation programs first.

563
00:48:01,640 --> 00:48:03,250
That's major boring shit.

564
00:48:03,250 --> 00:48:05,100
Let's do something a little more fun.

565
00:48:05,430 --> 00:48:06,930
How about...

566
00:48:08,480 --> 00:48:10,230
combat training?

567
00:48:16,280 --> 00:48:17,740
"Jujitsu"?

568
00:48:18,610 --> 00:48:20,280
I'm going to learn jujitsu?

569
00:48:31,630 --> 00:48:32,830
Holy shit!

571
00:48:35,750 --> 00:48:37,050
How about some more?

572
00:48:37,300 --> 00:48:38,590
Hell, yes.

573
00:48:40,590 --> 00:48:41,720
Hell, yeah.

578
00:48:53,810 --> 00:48:54,980
How is he?

579
00:48:55,230 --> 00:48:57,440
Ten hours straight. He's a machine.

580
00:49:08,620 --> 00:49:10,000
I know kung fu.

581
00:49:11,670 --> 00:49:12,710
Show me.

582
00:49:14,460 --> 00:49:16,210
This is a sparring program,

583
00:49:16,460 --> 00:49:19,260
similar to the programmed reality of the Matrix.

584
00:49:19,510 --> 00:49:21,840
It has the same basic rules. Rules like gravity.

585
00:49:22,090 --> 00:49:24,390
What you must learn is that these rules are no different than

586
00:49:24,390 --> 00:49:25,550
the rules of a computer system.

587
00:49:26,100 --> 00:49:27,600
Some of them can be bent.

588
00:49:27,810 --> 00:49:30,270
Others can be broken.

589
00:49:30,640 --> 00:49:31,890
Understand?

590
00:49:33,190 --> 00:49:35,730
Then hit me, if you can.

591
00:50:14,600 --> 00:50:15,770
Good!

592
00:50:16,520 --> 00:50:17,690
Adaptation.

593
00:50:17,980 --> 00:50:19,190
Improvisation.

594
00:50:19,480 --> 00:50:20,820
But your weakness

595
00:50:21,070 --> 00:50:22,440
is not your technique.

596
00:50:29,410 --> 00:50:31,500
Morpheus is fighting Neo.

597
00:51:43,780 --> 00:51:44,940
How did I beat you?

598
00:51:51,530 --> 00:51:52,620
You're too fast.

599
00:51:53,160 --> 00:51:54,490
Do you believe that

600
00:51:54,870 --> 00:51:57,370
my being stronger or faster

601
00:51:57,620 --> 00:52:01,290
has anything to do with my muscles in this place?

602
00:52:05,340 --> 00:52:07,130
You think that's air you're breathing now?

603
00:52:20,650 --> 00:52:21,860
Again!

604
00:52:33,330 --> 00:52:35,740
Jesus Christ, he's fast!

605
00:52:35,990 --> 00:52:38,210
Take a look at his neuro-kinetics, they are way above normal.

606
00:52:43,670 --> 00:52:45,130
What are you waiting for?

607
00:52:45,380 --> 00:52:47,340
You're faster than this.

608
00:52:49,550 --> 00:52:51,760
Don't think you are.

609
00:52:52,010 --> 00:52:53,680
Know you are.

610
00:53:04,060 --> 00:53:06,900
Come on! Stop trying to hit me, and hit me!

611
00:53:16,790 --> 00:53:18,540
I don't believe it.

612
00:53:20,080 --> 00:53:22,210
I know what you're trying to do.

613
00:53:23,880 --> 00:53:26,040
I'm trying to free your mind, Neo.

614
00:53:26,380 --> 00:53:28,460
But I can only show you the door.

615
00:53:29,050 --> 00:53:30,920
You are the one that has to walk through it.

616
00:53:33,260 --> 00:53:35,390
Tank, load the jump program.

617
00:53:46,980 --> 00:53:49,480
You have to let it all go, Neo.

618
00:53:49,490 --> 00:53:52,400
Fear, doubt and disbelief.

619
00:53:53,570 --> 00:53:56,280
Free your mind.

620
00:54:12,470 --> 00:54:14,180
Okey-dokey.

621
00:54:16,260 --> 00:54:17,430
Free my mind.

622
00:54:17,890 --> 00:54:19,010
What if he makes it?

623
00:54:19,260 --> 00:54:21,980
- No one's ever made their first jump. - I know, I know.

624
00:54:23,310 --> 00:54:25,770
- But what if he does? - He won't.

625
00:54:26,270 --> 00:54:27,440
Come on.

626
00:54:27,690 --> 00:54:28,860
All right.

627
00:54:29,320 --> 00:54:31,360
No problem. Free my mind.

628
00:54:32,150 --> 00:54:34,950
Free my mind. No problem. Right.

629
00:54:54,340 --> 00:54:56,010
What does that mean?

630
00:54:56,390 --> 00:54:58,220
It doesn't mean anything.

631
00:54:58,800 --> 00:55:01,390
Everybody falls the first time.

632
00:55:01,850 --> 00:55:03,140
Right, Trin?

633
00:55:23,830 --> 00:55:25,530
I thought it wasn't real.

634
00:55:25,530 --> 00:55:26,460
Your mind makes it real.

635
00:55:29,710 --> 00:55:33,170
If you're killed in the Matrix, you die here?

636
00:55:33,800 --> 00:55:36,260
The body cannot live without the mind.

637
00:56:06,750 --> 00:56:10,130
I don't remember you ever bringing me dinner.

638
00:56:13,210 --> 00:56:16,050
There is something about him, isn't there?

639
00:56:16,670 --> 00:56:18,300
Don't tell me you're a believer now?

640
00:56:19,300 --> 00:56:20,510
I just keep wondering

641
00:56:20,760 --> 00:56:22,260
if Morpheus is so sure,

642
00:56:22,260 --> 00:56:24,430
why isn't he take him to see the Oracle?

643
00:56:25,350 --> 00:56:28,270
Morpheus will take him when he's ready.

644
00:56:38,070 --> 00:56:39,610
The Matrix is a system, Neo.

645
00:56:41,370 --> 00:56:42,660
That system is our enemy.

646
00:56:43,280 --> 00:56:45,620
But when you're inside, look around, what do you see?

647
00:56:45,870 --> 00:56:49,670
Businessmen, teachers, lawyers, carpenters.

648
00:56:50,120 --> 00:56:52,710
The very minds of the people we are trying to save.

649
00:56:52,960 --> 00:56:55,920
But until we do, these people are a part of that system,

650
00:56:56,170 --> 00:56:58,670
and that makes them our enemy.

651
00:56:58,720 --> 00:56:59,550
You have to understand,

652
00:56:59,720 --> 00:57:03,050
most of these people are not ready to be unplugged.

653
00:57:03,300 --> 00:57:04,890
And many of them are so inert

654
00:57:05,140 --> 00:57:07,560
so hopelessly dependent on the system

655
00:57:07,810 --> 00:57:10,520
that they will fight to protect it.

656
00:57:12,020 --> 00:57:13,410
Were you listening to me Neo,

657
00:57:13,410 --> 00:57:15,770
or were you looking at the woman in the red dress?

658
00:57:16,650 --> 00:57:17,690
- I was... - Look again.

659
00:57:18,940 --> 00:57:20,030
Freeze it.

660
00:57:23,990 --> 00:57:26,430
This...

661
00:57:26,660 --> 00:57:28,290
- This isn't the Matrix? - No.

662
00:57:30,080 --> 00:57:31,340
It's another training program

663
00:57:31,340 --> 00:57:33,920
designed to teach you one thing:

664
00:57:34,540 --> 00:57:36,960
If you are not one of us, you are one of them.

665
00:57:37,500 --> 00:57:40,300
- What are they? - Sentient programs.

666
00:57:41,050 --> 00:57:42,660
They can move in and out of

667
00:57:42,660 --> 00:57:45,350
any software still hardwired to their system.

668
00:57:45,720 --> 00:57:49,100
That means that anyone we haven't unplugged

669
00:57:49,430 --> 00:57:50,770
is potentially an agent.

670
00:57:51,730 --> 00:57:53,560
Inside the Matrix

671
00:57:54,150 --> 00:57:55,860
they are everyone,

672
00:57:56,190 --> 00:57:57,900
and they are no one.

673
00:57:58,150 --> 00:58:01,280
We have survived by hiding and running from them,

674
00:58:01,530 --> 00:58:03,160
but they are the gatekeepers.

675
00:58:03,410 --> 00:58:06,370
They're guarding all the doors, they're holding all the keys.

676
00:58:06,620 --> 00:58:09,450
Which means that sooner or later, someone will have to fight them.

677
00:58:09,620 --> 00:58:10,830
Someone?

678
00:58:11,160 --> 00:58:12,580
I won't lie to you, Neo.

679
00:58:13,040 --> 00:58:14,770
Every single man or woman who has stood their ground,

680
00:58:14,770 --> 00:58:17,880
everyone who has fought an agent has died.

681
00:58:18,130 --> 00:58:20,510
But where they have failed, you will succeed.

682
00:58:20,710 --> 00:58:21,760
Why?

683
00:58:22,010 --> 00:58:24,300
I've seen an agent punch through a concrete wall.

684
00:58:24,550 --> 00:58:28,140
Men have emptied entire clips at them and hit nothing but air.

685
00:58:28,390 --> 00:58:30,240
Yet their strength and their speed

686
00:58:30,240 --> 00:58:33,020
are still based in a world that is built on rules.

687
00:58:33,270 --> 00:58:34,390
Because of that,

688
00:58:34,650 --> 00:58:38,020
they will never be as strong or as fast as you can be.

689
00:58:42,320 --> 00:58:44,200
What are you telling me?

690
00:58:44,910 --> 00:58:46,370
That I can dodge bullets?

691
00:58:48,370 --> 00:58:49,740
No, Neo.

692
00:58:50,240 --> 00:58:53,160
I'm trying to tell you that when you're ready,

693
00:58:54,040 --> 00:58:55,420
you won't have to.

694
00:58:59,710 --> 00:59:00,750
We got trouble.

695
00:59:19,650 --> 00:59:22,110
- Did Zion send the warning? - No, another ship.

696
00:59:25,360 --> 00:59:26,660
Shit.

697
00:59:26,910 --> 00:59:29,780
- Squiddy's sweeping in quick. - Squiddy?

698
00:59:29,990 --> 00:59:33,200
A sentinel. A killing machine designed for one thing.

699
00:59:33,450 --> 00:59:34,660
Search and destroy.

700
00:59:36,000 --> 00:59:37,170
Set her down there.

701
00:59:58,980 --> 01:00:01,110
How are we doing, Tank?

702
01:00:08,660 --> 01:00:09,820
Power off-line.

703
01:00:10,320 --> 01:00:14,370
- EMP armed... and ready. - EMP?

704
01:00:14,660 --> 01:00:16,540
Electromagnetic pulse.

705
01:00:16,790 --> 01:00:19,670
Disables any electrical system in the blast radius.

706
01:00:19,920 --> 01:00:22,130
It's the only weapon we have against the machines.

707
01:00:27,930 --> 01:00:31,050
- Where are we? - Their old service and waste systems.

708
01:00:32,390 --> 01:00:33,430
Sewers.

709
01:00:33,640 --> 01:00:36,350
There used to be cities that spanned hundreds of miles.

710
01:00:36,850 --> 01:00:38,770
Now these sewers are all that's left.

711
01:00:39,020 --> 01:00:40,350
Quiet.

712
01:01:21,520 --> 01:01:26,400
Neo. You scared the bejesus out of me.

713
01:01:27,480 --> 01:01:29,400
- Sorry. - It's okay.

714
01:01:32,320 --> 01:01:34,990
- Is that...? - The Matrix? Yeah.

715
01:01:38,160 --> 01:01:41,330
- Do you always look at it encoded? - Well, you have to.

716
01:01:41,580 --> 01:01:44,670
The image translators work for the construct program.

717
01:01:44,920 --> 01:01:48,340
But there's way too much information to decode the Matrix.

718
01:01:48,590 --> 01:01:51,550
You get used to it. I don't even see the code.

719
01:01:51,800 --> 01:01:55,220
All I see is blonde, brunette, redhead.

720
01:01:56,390 --> 01:01:59,140
You, uh, you want a drink?

721
01:01:59,390 --> 01:02:00,430
Sure.

722
01:02:03,980 --> 01:02:07,900
You know, I know what you're thinking.

723
01:02:08,150 --> 01:02:10,280
Because right now I'm thinking the same thing.

724
01:02:10,570 --> 01:02:13,910
Actually, I've been thinking it ever since I got here.

725
01:02:15,820 --> 01:02:18,830
Why, oh, why didn't I take the blue pill?

726
01:02:31,210 --> 01:02:33,130
Good shit, huh?

727
01:02:33,470 --> 01:02:34,680
Dozer makes it.

728
01:02:35,140 --> 01:02:36,300
It's good for two things:

729
01:02:36,550 --> 01:02:39,640
Degreasing engines and killing brain cells.

730
01:02:40,640 --> 01:02:42,850
So can I ask you something?

731
01:02:45,850 --> 01:02:47,480
Did he tell you why he did it?

732
01:02:50,110 --> 01:02:51,940
Why you're here?

733
01:02:55,610 --> 01:02:57,370
Jesus!

734
01:02:58,580 --> 01:03:00,490
What a mind job!

735
01:03:01,910 --> 01:03:04,710
So you're here to save the world.

736
01:03:06,210 --> 01:03:08,290
What do you say to something like that?

737
01:03:13,470 --> 01:03:14,840
A little piece of advice.

738
01:03:16,640 --> 01:03:20,680
You see an agent, you do what we do:

739
01:03:21,010 --> 01:03:22,560
Run.

740
01:03:22,890 --> 01:03:24,640
You run your ass off.

741
01:03:31,900 --> 01:03:33,610
Thanks for the drink.

742
01:03:38,320 --> 01:03:39,490
Sweet dreams.

743
01:03:43,500 --> 01:03:46,920
Do we have a deal, Mr. Reagan?

744
01:03:47,580 --> 01:03:52,590
You know, I know this steak doesn't exist.

745
01:03:53,590 --> 01:03:56,340
I know that when I put it in my mouth,

746
01:03:56,590 --> 01:03:59,680
the Matrix is telling my brain that it is,

747
01:03:59,970 --> 01:04:03,100
juicy, and delicious.

748
01:04:06,020 --> 01:04:09,860
After nine years, you know what I realize?

749
01:04:17,700 --> 01:04:18,910
Ignorance is bliss.

750
01:04:23,950 --> 01:04:25,790
Then we have a deal.

751
01:04:28,290 --> 01:04:30,210
I don't want to remember nothing.

752
01:04:30,460 --> 01:04:33,000
Nothing. You understand?

753
01:04:37,050 --> 01:04:38,840
And I want to be rich.

754
01:04:40,180 --> 01:04:42,890
You know, someone important.

755
01:04:44,390 --> 01:04:45,520
Like an actor.

756
01:04:46,730 --> 01:04:49,850
Whatever you want, Mr. Reagan.

757
01:04:52,020 --> 01:04:53,570
Okay.

758
01:04:53,940 --> 01:04:56,360
You get my body back in a power plant,

759
01:04:56,740 --> 01:04:58,490
reinsert me into the Matrix,

760
01:04:58,820 --> 01:05:00,240
I'll get you what you want.

761
01:05:00,490 --> 01:05:02,490
Access codes to the Zion mainframe.

762
01:05:02,740 --> 01:05:04,910
No. I told you, I don't know them.

763
01:05:07,870 --> 01:05:09,870
I can get you the man who does.

764
01:05:10,620 --> 01:05:12,420
Morpheus.

765
01:05:22,510 --> 01:05:25,970
Here you go, buddy. Breakfast of champions.

766
01:05:27,310 --> 01:05:30,100
Close your eyes, it feels like you're eating runny eggs.

767
01:05:30,350 --> 01:05:32,350
Or a bowl of snot.

768
01:05:32,560 --> 01:05:34,150
You know what it reminds me of?

769
01:05:35,980 --> 01:05:38,320
Tastee Wheat. Did you ever eat Tastee Wheat?

770
01:05:38,940 --> 01:05:40,650
No, but technically, neither did you.

771
01:05:40,900 --> 01:05:42,950
That's exactly my point. Exactly.

772
01:05:43,200 --> 01:05:44,580
Because you have to wonder, now,

773
01:05:44,830 --> 01:05:48,080
how do the machines really know what Tastee Wheat tasted like?

774
01:05:48,330 --> 01:05:49,750
Maybe they got it wrong.

775
01:05:50,000 --> 01:05:51,210
Maybe what I think Tastee Wheat tasted like

776
01:05:51,210 --> 01:05:55,500
actually tasted like oatmeal or tuna fish.

777
01:05:55,880 --> 01:05:57,390
That makes you wonder about a lot of things.

778
01:05:57,390 --> 01:05:58,710
You take chicken for example,

779
01:05:58,960 --> 01:06:00,970
maybe they couldn't figure out what to make chicken taste like,

780
01:06:01,220 --> 01:06:03,260
which is why chicken tastes like everything.

781
01:06:03,510 --> 01:06:05,300
- And maybe they... - Shut up, Mouse.

782
01:06:06,930 --> 01:06:08,390
It's a single-celled protein

783
01:06:08,640 --> 01:06:11,690
combined with synthetic aminos, vitamins and minerals.

784
01:06:11,940 --> 01:06:13,190
Everything the body needs.

785
01:06:13,440 --> 01:06:16,320
It doesn't have everything the body needs.

786
01:06:19,070 --> 01:06:22,150
I understand you've run through the agent training program.

787
01:06:23,200 --> 01:06:25,240
You know, I wrote that program.

788
01:06:25,530 --> 01:06:26,830
Here it comes.

789
01:06:27,080 --> 01:06:29,040
- So what did you think of her? - Of who?

790
01:06:29,410 --> 01:06:32,460
The woman in the red dress. I designed her.

791
01:06:32,790 --> 01:06:35,540
She doesn't talk very much,

792
01:06:35,790 --> 01:06:37,660
but... but if you'd like to meet her,

793
01:06:37,660 --> 01:06:39,760
I can arrange a much more personalized meeting.

794
01:06:40,010 --> 01:06:41,380
The digital pimp hard at work.

795
01:06:41,630 --> 01:06:43,880
Pay no attention to these hypocrites, Neo.

796
01:06:45,180 --> 01:06:47,010
To deny our own impulses

797
01:06:47,260 --> 01:06:50,390
is to deny the very thing that makes us human.

798
01:06:52,310 --> 01:06:53,690
Dozer, when you're done,

799
01:06:53,940 --> 01:06:55,350
bring the ship up to broadcast depth.

800
01:06:56,060 --> 01:06:57,400
We're going in.

801
01:06:58,110 --> 01:06:59,520
I'm taking Neo to see her.

802
01:07:03,650 --> 01:07:04,700
See who?

803
01:07:05,700 --> 01:07:06,950
The Oracle.

804
01:07:12,450 --> 01:07:14,000
Everyone, please observe

805
01:07:14,330 --> 01:07:17,040
the "Fasten seat belt" and "No smoking" signs have been turned on.

806
01:07:17,540 --> 01:07:20,920
Sit back and enjoy your flight.

807
01:07:45,240 --> 01:07:46,280
We're in.

808
01:08:02,000 --> 01:08:03,130
We'll be back in an hour.

809
01:08:17,940 --> 01:08:21,520
Unbelievable, isn't it?

810
01:08:25,110 --> 01:08:26,950
- God! - What?

811
01:08:27,610 --> 01:08:28,990
I used to eat there.

812
01:08:31,240 --> 01:08:32,870
Really good noodles.

813
01:08:37,660 --> 01:08:40,170
I have these memories from my life.

814
01:08:42,630 --> 01:08:44,300
None of them happened.

815
01:08:44,920 --> 01:08:46,260
What does that mean?

816
01:08:46,510 --> 01:08:48,720
That the Matrix cannot tell you who you are.

817
01:08:49,640 --> 01:08:50,840
But the Oracle can?

818
01:08:51,300 --> 01:08:52,510
That's different.

819
01:08:57,270 --> 01:08:59,440
Did you go to her?

820
01:09:00,020 --> 01:09:01,190
Yes.

821
01:09:01,690 --> 01:09:03,070
What did she tell you?

822
01:09:06,320 --> 01:09:07,820
She told me...

823
01:09:08,860 --> 01:09:10,030
What?

824
01:09:13,830 --> 01:09:15,160
We're here.

825
01:09:15,320 --> 01:09:17,830
Neo, come with me.

826
01:09:37,810 --> 01:09:41,650
So is this the same Oracle that made the prophecy?

827
01:09:41,900 --> 01:09:44,330
Yes. She's very old.

828
01:09:44,330 --> 01:09:46,230
She's been with us since the beginning.

829
01:09:46,690 --> 01:09:48,690
- The beginning? - Of the Resistance.

830
01:09:50,950 --> 01:09:53,320
And she knows what? Everything?

831
01:09:55,370 --> 01:09:57,290
She would say she knows enough.

832
01:09:58,410 --> 01:10:00,210
And she's never wrong.

833
01:10:02,420 --> 01:10:05,590
Try not to think of it in terms of right and wrong.

834
01:10:05,920 --> 01:10:07,500
She is a guide, Neo.

835
01:10:07,880 --> 01:10:09,760
She can help you to find the path.

836
01:10:10,340 --> 01:10:13,170
- She helped you? - Yes.

837
01:10:14,010 --> 01:10:15,350
What did she tell you?

838
01:10:17,810 --> 01:10:20,020
That I would find the One.

839
01:10:33,160 --> 01:10:35,280
I told you I can only show you the door.

840
01:10:35,990 --> 01:10:38,080
You have to walk through it.

841
01:10:41,870 --> 01:10:42,960
Hello, Neo.

842
01:10:43,210 --> 01:10:44,880
You're right on time.

843
01:10:52,800 --> 01:10:56,600
Make yourself at home, Morpheus. Neo, come with me.

844
01:11:02,270 --> 01:11:03,850
These are the other Potentials.

845
01:11:04,100 --> 01:11:05,650
You can wait here.

846
01:11:46,480 --> 01:11:49,020
Do not try and bend the spoon.

847
01:11:49,400 --> 01:11:51,530
That's impossible.

848
01:11:52,360 --> 01:11:56,360
Instead, only try to realize the truth.

849
01:11:56,910 --> 01:11:58,280
What truth?

850
01:11:58,530 --> 01:12:00,200
There is no spoon.

851
01:12:02,790 --> 01:12:04,120
There is no spoon?

852
01:12:04,370 --> 01:12:06,000
Then you'll see that

853
01:12:06,000 --> 01:12:08,880
it is not the spoon that bends. It is only yourself.

854
01:12:24,890 --> 01:12:26,390
The Oracle will you see now.

855
01:12:37,070 --> 01:12:38,610
I know you're Neo.

856
01:12:39,240 --> 01:12:40,410
Be right with you.

857
01:12:41,450 --> 01:12:43,830
- You're the Oracle? - Bingo.

858
01:12:46,540 --> 01:12:49,420
Not quite what you were expecting, right?

859
01:12:50,460 --> 01:12:52,630
Almost done.

860
01:12:55,130 --> 01:12:56,760
Smell good, don't they?

861
01:12:59,510 --> 01:13:01,350
I'd ask you to sit down...

862
01:13:01,600 --> 01:13:03,970
but you're not going to anyway.

863
01:13:04,470 --> 01:13:07,350
- And don't worry about the vase. - What vase?

864
01:13:10,480 --> 01:13:11,650
That vase.

865
01:13:12,610 --> 01:13:13,650
I'm sorry.

866
01:13:13,900 --> 01:13:15,780
I said, don't worry about it.

867
01:13:16,940 --> 01:13:18,900
I'll get one of my kids to fix it.

868
01:13:19,530 --> 01:13:20,740
How did you know?

869
01:13:22,780 --> 01:13:26,580
What's really going to bake your noodle later on is

870
01:13:26,910 --> 01:13:29,870
would you still have broken it if I hadn't said anything?

871
01:13:34,670 --> 01:13:36,590
You're cuter than I thought.

872
01:13:39,630 --> 01:13:41,890
I can see why she likes you.

873
01:13:42,760 --> 01:13:43,850
Who?

874
01:13:44,100 --> 01:13:45,930
Not too bright, though.

875
01:13:49,230 --> 01:13:52,310
You know why Morpheus brought you to see me.

876
01:13:54,440 --> 01:13:55,610
So...

877
01:13:56,570 --> 01:13:57,940
what do you think?

878
01:13:59,780 --> 01:14:01,530
Do you think you are the One?

879
01:14:03,490 --> 01:14:04,530
Honestly, I don't know.

880
01:14:07,950 --> 01:14:09,370
You know what that means?

882
01:14:11,750 --> 01:14:13,960
Means, "Know thyself."

883
01:14:15,420 --> 01:14:17,380
I'll let you in on a little secret.

884
01:14:19,630 --> 01:14:23,470
Being the One is just like being in love.

885
01:14:24,180 --> 01:14:27,060
No one can tell you you're in love. You just know it

886
01:14:27,310 --> 01:14:28,430
through and through.

887
01:14:28,770 --> 01:14:30,810
Balls to bones.

888
01:14:33,350 --> 01:14:35,230
Well,

889
01:14:36,150 --> 01:14:38,230
I'd better have a look at you.

890
01:14:39,570 --> 01:14:41,070
Open your mouth. Say, "Ah."

891
01:14:55,460 --> 01:14:57,130
Okay...

892
01:14:57,750 --> 01:15:02,720
Now I'm supposed to say, "Hmm, that's interesting, but..."

893
01:15:03,220 --> 01:15:04,340
Then you say:

894
01:15:04,930 --> 01:15:06,220
But what?

895
01:15:06,470 --> 01:15:10,430
But you already know what I'm going to tell you.

896
01:15:11,850 --> 01:15:14,810
- I'm not the One. - Sorry, kid.

897
01:15:16,440 --> 01:15:18,440
You got the gift

898
01:15:19,440 --> 01:15:21,650
but it looks like you're waiting for something.

899
01:15:26,530 --> 01:15:30,490
- What? - Your next life, maybe. Who knows?

900
01:15:31,080 --> 01:15:33,330
That's the way these things go.

901
01:15:34,210 --> 01:15:36,790
- What's funny? - Morpheus.

902
01:15:40,250 --> 01:15:41,960
He almost had me convinced.

903
01:15:42,210 --> 01:15:43,340
I know.

904
01:15:44,880 --> 01:15:47,010
Poor Morpheus.

905
01:15:49,390 --> 01:15:52,520
Without him, we're lost.

906
01:15:54,060 --> 01:15:56,230
What do you mean, "without him"?

907
01:16:00,230 --> 01:16:02,150
Are you sure you want to hear this?

908
01:16:04,360 --> 01:16:07,110
Morpheus believes in you, Neo.

909
01:16:08,820 --> 01:16:10,990
And no one, not you, not even me

910
01:16:11,240 --> 01:16:13,500
can convince him otherwise.

911
01:16:13,870 --> 01:16:16,250
He believes it so blindly

912
01:16:16,540 --> 01:16:20,880
that he's going to sacrifice his life to save yours.

913
01:16:21,130 --> 01:16:25,090
- What? - You're going to have to make a choice.

914
01:16:25,720 --> 01:16:29,300
In the one hand, you'll have Morpheus' life.

915
01:16:29,800 --> 01:16:32,680
And in the other hand, you'll have your own.

916
01:16:34,100 --> 01:16:36,390
One of you is going to die.

917
01:16:38,480 --> 01:16:41,770
Which one will be up to you.

918
01:16:43,150 --> 01:16:45,070
I'm sorry, kiddo. I really am.

919
01:16:45,320 --> 01:16:46,990
You have a good soul.

920
01:16:48,070 --> 01:16:50,780
And I hate giving good people bad news.

921
01:16:53,910 --> 01:16:55,370
Don't worry about it.

922
01:16:55,620 --> 01:16:58,040
As soon as you step outside that door

923
01:16:58,290 --> 01:17:00,420
you'll start feeling better.

924
01:17:01,130 --> 01:17:04,920
You'll remember you don't believe in any of this fate crap.

925
01:17:05,760 --> 01:17:08,510
You're in control of your own life.

926
01:17:09,340 --> 01:17:10,640
Remember?

927
01:17:12,510 --> 01:17:14,180
Here,

928
01:17:15,390 --> 01:17:16,930
take a cookie.

929
01:17:17,480 --> 01:17:20,810
I promise, by the time you're done eating it

930
01:17:21,770 --> 01:17:24,150
you'll feel right as rain.

931
01:17:33,370 --> 01:17:34,700
What was said

932
01:17:35,330 --> 01:17:36,790
was for you

933
01:17:37,330 --> 01:17:39,160
and for you alone.

935
01:18:02,100 --> 01:18:03,230
They're on their way.

936
01:18:33,010 --> 01:18:34,050
What is that?

937
01:18:48,820 --> 01:18:50,240
Oh, deja vu.

938
01:18:53,740 --> 01:18:54,820
What did you just say?

939
01:18:55,070 --> 01:18:56,580
Nothing. Just having a little deja vu.

940
01:18:56,830 --> 01:18:58,450
- What did you see? - What happened?

941
01:18:59,870 --> 01:19:02,040
A black cat went past us,

942
01:19:02,290 --> 01:19:03,920
then another just like it.

943
01:19:04,170 --> 01:19:05,710
How much like it? Was it the same cat?

944
01:19:06,670 --> 01:19:07,880
Might have been. I'm not sure.

945
01:19:08,670 --> 01:19:10,460
Switch, Apoc.

946
01:19:13,760 --> 01:19:14,800
What is it?

947
01:19:15,050 --> 01:19:16,440
A deja vu is usually a

948
01:19:16,440 --> 01:19:18,500
glitch in the Matrix which happens

949
01:19:18,500 --> 01:19:19,470
when they change something.

950
01:19:22,640 --> 01:19:23,690
Oh, my God.

951
01:19:25,520 --> 01:19:27,610
Let's go.

952
01:19:31,740 --> 01:19:33,490
They cut the hard line. It's a trap! Get out!

953
01:19:39,030 --> 01:19:40,240
Oh, no.

954
01:19:41,700 --> 01:19:42,750
Oh, no.

955
01:20:20,530 --> 01:20:23,000
That's what they changed. We're trapped. There's no way out.

956
01:20:23,250 --> 01:20:25,120
Be calm. Give me your phone.

957
01:20:25,370 --> 01:20:26,920
They'll be able to track it.

958
01:20:27,170 --> 01:20:28,580
We have no choice.

959
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:31,210
Operator.

960
01:20:31,550 --> 01:20:34,380
Tank, find a structural drawing of this building, Find it fast.

961
01:20:42,220 --> 01:20:44,810
- Got it! - I need the main wet-wall.

963
01:20:47,810 --> 01:20:48,900
Eighth floor.

964
01:20:49,100 --> 01:20:50,690
They're on the eighth floor.

965
01:20:50,980 --> 01:20:52,440
Switch, straight ahead.

966
01:20:53,090 --> 01:20:54,450
Neo.

967
01:21:00,490 --> 01:21:02,660
I hope the Oracle gave you some good news.

968
01:21:10,920 --> 01:21:12,420
Now left, That's it,

969
01:21:12,710 --> 01:21:13,750
Good.

970
01:21:23,470 --> 01:21:24,770
Where are they?

971
01:22:25,200 --> 01:22:26,370
They're in the walls.

972
01:22:27,830 --> 01:22:29,000
In the walls!

973
01:22:50,390 --> 01:22:52,100
It's an agent!

974
01:22:58,410 --> 01:23:00,260
Morpheus!

975
01:23:01,030 --> 01:23:04,200
You must get Neo out! He's all that matters!

976
01:23:04,490 --> 01:23:05,700
No, Morpheus! Don't!

977
01:23:05,950 --> 01:23:07,490
Trinity, go!

978
01:23:07,660 --> 01:23:09,040
Go!

979
01:23:15,250 --> 01:23:17,170
- We can't leave him! - We have to!

980
01:23:42,440 --> 01:23:44,450
Cypher! Come on!

981
01:23:48,200 --> 01:23:52,040
The great Morpheus. We meet at last.

982
01:23:52,580 --> 01:23:53,710
And you are?

983
01:23:53,960 --> 01:23:55,710
A Smith.

984
01:23:55,960 --> 01:23:57,250
Agent Smith.

985
01:23:57,830 --> 01:23:59,880
You all look the same to me.

986
01:24:55,520 --> 01:24:56,810
Take him.

987
01:25:03,320 --> 01:25:04,330
No!

988
01:25:10,030 --> 01:25:11,870
- Operator. - I need an exit, fast,

989
01:25:13,950 --> 01:25:16,870
There was an accident. Goddamn car accident.

990
01:25:17,210 --> 01:25:19,000
All of a sudden, boom,

991
01:25:19,250 --> 01:25:20,630
somebody up there still likes me.

992
01:25:20,880 --> 01:25:22,130
I got you.

993
01:25:22,630 --> 01:25:24,550
Just get me out of here fast.

994
01:25:24,800 --> 01:25:26,680
Nearest exit, Franklin and Erie.

995
01:25:26,680 --> 01:25:27,470
An old TV repair shop.

996
01:25:27,720 --> 01:25:28,760
Right.

997
01:25:31,890 --> 01:25:33,470
- Operator. - Tank, it's me,

998
01:25:33,720 --> 01:25:34,890
Is Morpheus alive?

999
01:25:35,270 --> 01:25:36,560
Is Morpheus alive, Tank?

1000
01:25:36,980 --> 01:25:38,890
Yes, They're moving him, I don't know where to yet.

1001
01:25:39,100 --> 01:25:41,310
He's alive. We need an exit.

1002
01:25:41,310 --> 01:25:42,560
You're not far from Cypher.

1003
01:25:42,810 --> 01:25:44,150
- Cypher? - I know.

1004
01:25:44,400 --> 01:25:46,250
I sent him to Franklin and Erie.

1005
01:25:46,250 --> 01:25:46,490
Got it.

1006
01:25:55,580 --> 01:25:56,790
Got him.

1007
01:26:07,710 --> 01:26:08,760
Where are they?

1008
01:26:09,010 --> 01:26:10,260
Making the call.

1009
01:26:10,930 --> 01:26:12,090
Good.

1010
01:26:25,650 --> 01:26:27,440
You first, Neo.

1011
01:26:29,650 --> 01:26:30,900
Shit!

1012
01:26:39,580 --> 01:26:41,750
I don't know. It just went dead.

1013
01:27:08,570 --> 01:27:09,780
Hello, Trinity.

1014
01:27:10,190 --> 01:27:11,530
Cypher? Where's Tank?

1015
01:27:17,120 --> 01:27:18,160
You know

1016
01:27:19,870 --> 01:27:22,000
for a long time

1017
01:27:23,210 --> 01:27:26,130
I thought I was in love with you.

1018
01:27:26,880 --> 01:27:28,920
I used to dream about you.

1019
01:27:30,010 --> 01:27:32,720
You're a beautiful woman, Trinity.

1020
01:27:32,970 --> 01:27:35,340
Too bad things had to turn out this way.

1021
01:27:35,840 --> 01:27:36,930
You killed them.

1022
01:27:37,430 --> 01:27:38,930
- What? - Oh, God.

1023
01:27:39,180 --> 01:27:40,600
I'm tired, Trinity.

1024
01:27:42,020 --> 01:27:43,890
I'm tired of this war

1025
01:27:44,190 --> 01:27:47,020
tired of fighting. I'm tired of this ship

1026
01:27:47,360 --> 01:27:51,990
of being cold, of eating the same goddamn goop every day.

1027
01:27:54,280 --> 01:27:55,320
But most of all

1028
01:27:55,910 --> 01:27:59,280
I'm tired of that jackoff and all of his bullshit.

1029
01:28:00,410 --> 01:28:01,700
Surprise, asshole!

1030
01:28:02,250 --> 01:28:04,460
I bet you never saw this coming,

1031
01:28:04,710 --> 01:28:05,750
did you?

1032
01:28:08,040 --> 01:28:10,420
God, I wish I could be there

1033
01:28:11,000 --> 01:28:12,510
when they break you.

1034
01:28:13,550 --> 01:28:16,720
I wish I could walk in just when it happens

1035
01:28:17,430 --> 01:28:19,140
so right then

1036
01:28:19,390 --> 01:28:20,720
you'd know it was me.

1037
01:28:21,140 --> 01:28:24,100
- You gave them Morpheus. - He lied to us, Trinity.

1038
01:28:24,690 --> 01:28:26,190
He tricked us!

1039
01:28:26,730 --> 01:28:28,730
If you had told us the truth

1040
01:28:28,980 --> 01:28:31,860
we would've told you to shove that red pill up your ass!

1041
01:28:32,110 --> 01:28:34,950
That is not true, Cypher. He set us free.

1042
01:28:34,960 --> 01:28:35,400
"Free".

1043
01:28:35,650 --> 01:28:37,360
You call this free?

1044
01:28:39,780 --> 01:28:42,290
All I do is what he tells me to do.

1045
01:28:43,870 --> 01:28:46,790
If I had to choose between that and the Matrix,

1046
01:28:47,960 --> 01:28:49,170
I choose the Matrix.

1047
01:28:49,420 --> 01:28:51,090
The Matrix isn't real.

1048
01:28:51,340 --> 01:28:52,750
I disagree, Trinity.

1049
01:28:53,010 --> 01:28:55,260
I think the Matrix

1050
01:28:55,590 --> 01:28:58,180
can be more real than this world.

1051
01:29:00,350 --> 01:29:02,850
All I do is pull the plug here.

1052
01:29:03,100 --> 01:29:04,430
But there

1053
01:29:04,980 --> 01:29:07,270
you have to watch Apoc die.

1054
01:29:08,130 --> 01:29:09,730
Trinity.

1055
01:29:11,390 --> 01:29:12,760
No!

1056
01:29:15,030 --> 01:29:16,740
Welcome to the real world, lady.

1057
01:29:16,900 --> 01:29:17,990
But you're out, Cypher.

1058
01:29:18,240 --> 01:29:20,660
- You can't go back. - Oh, no. That's what you think.

1059
01:29:20,910 --> 01:29:22,410
They're gonnal reinsert my body,

1060
01:29:22,660 --> 01:29:24,000
I go back to sleep,

1061
01:29:24,000 --> 01:29:26,290
and when I wake up, I won't remember a goddamn thing,

1062
01:29:26,540 --> 01:29:27,660
By the way

1063
01:29:27,830 --> 01:29:30,750
if you have anything terribly important to say to Switch,

1064
01:29:31,250 --> 01:29:33,460
- I suggest you say it now, - No, please don't.

1065
01:29:34,000 --> 01:29:35,630
Not like this.

1066
01:29:37,340 --> 01:29:38,970
Not like this.

1067
01:29:43,430 --> 01:29:44,470
Too late.

1068
01:29:44,930 --> 01:29:46,520
Goddamn you, Cypher!

1069
01:29:46,770 --> 01:29:48,640
Don't hate me, Trinity.

1070
01:29:49,020 --> 01:29:50,900
I'm just a messenger.

1071
01:29:51,310 --> 01:29:54,480
And right now, I'm going to prove it to you.

1072
01:29:55,570 --> 01:29:57,240
If Morpheus was right.

1073
01:29:57,780 --> 01:29:59,660
there's no way I can pull this plug.

1074
01:30:00,240 --> 01:30:01,740
If Neo's the One,

1075
01:30:02,240 --> 01:30:04,080
then there'd have to be

1076
01:30:04,330 --> 01:30:06,910
some kind of a miracle to stop me.

1077
01:30:07,410 --> 01:30:08,750
Right?

1078
01:30:08,910 --> 01:30:12,250
I mean, how can he be the One if he's dead?

1079
01:30:13,630 --> 01:30:15,880
You never did answer me before,

1080
01:30:16,170 --> 01:30:18,510
if you bought into Morpheus' bullshit.

1081
01:30:18,880 --> 01:30:22,090
Come on. All I want is a little yes or no.

1082
01:30:23,470 --> 01:30:25,810
Look into his eyes,

1083
01:30:26,560 --> 01:30:28,060
those big, pretty eyes

1084
01:30:30,810 --> 01:30:32,150
and tell me

1085
01:30:32,850 --> 01:30:34,150
yes

1086
01:30:34,440 --> 01:30:35,820
or no,

1087
01:30:37,110 --> 01:30:38,240
Yes.

1088
01:30:38,860 --> 01:30:39,990
No, I don't believe it.

1089
01:30:41,410 --> 01:30:44,500
Believe it or not, you piece of shit,

1090
01:30:44,500 --> 01:30:46,160
you're still going to burn!

1091
01:31:04,550 --> 01:31:05,800
You first.

1092
01:31:13,850 --> 01:31:14,900
You're hurt.

1093
01:31:15,230 --> 01:31:16,320
I'll be all right.

1094
01:31:19,110 --> 01:31:20,280
Dozer?

1095
01:31:38,550 --> 01:31:40,920
Have you ever stood and stared at it?

1096
01:31:41,800 --> 01:31:44,930
Marveled at its beauty

1097
01:31:45,300 --> 01:31:47,550
its genius?

1098
01:31:48,720 --> 01:31:50,600
Billions of people

1099
01:31:50,850 --> 01:31:53,600
just living out their lives.

1100
01:31:54,650 --> 01:31:56,310
Oblivious.

1101
01:32:00,900 --> 01:32:03,780
Did you know that the first Matrix

1102
01:32:04,030 --> 01:32:05,700
was designed to be a

1103
01:32:05,700 --> 01:32:08,740
perfect human world where none suffered

1104
01:32:09,200 --> 01:32:12,120
where everyone would be happy.

1105
01:32:12,660 --> 01:32:14,160
It was a disaster.

1106
01:32:14,410 --> 01:32:18,750
No one would accept the program. Entire crops were lost.

1107
01:32:19,630 --> 01:32:21,380
Some believe that

1108
01:32:21,630 --> 01:32:23,430
we lacked the programming language

1109
01:32:23,430 --> 01:32:26,010
to describe your perfect world.

1110
01:32:26,260 --> 01:32:29,140
But I believe that, as a species

1111
01:32:29,390 --> 01:32:33,230
human beings define their reality through misery...

1112
01:32:33,480 --> 01:32:34,850
and suffering.

1113
01:32:35,100 --> 01:32:37,810
So the perfect world was a dream

1114
01:32:38,060 --> 01:32:42,900
that your primitive cerebrum kept trying to wake up from.

1115
01:32:44,240 --> 01:32:47,910
Which is why the Matrix was redesigned to this.

1116
01:32:48,370 --> 01:32:51,540
The peak of your civilization.

1117
01:32:51,790 --> 01:32:54,040
I say, "your civilization"

1118
01:32:54,290 --> 01:32:56,780
because as soon as we started thinking for you,

1119
01:32:56,780 --> 01:32:58,420
it became our civilization

1120
01:32:58,670 --> 01:33:01,750
which is, of course, what this is all about.

1121
01:33:03,090 --> 01:33:05,670
Evolution, Morpheus.

1122
01:33:05,970 --> 01:33:07,300
Evolution.

1123
01:33:09,600 --> 01:33:11,470
Like the dinosaur.

1124
01:33:13,640 --> 01:33:15,270
Look out that window.

1125
01:33:15,980 --> 01:33:18,100
You had your time.

1126
01:33:18,810 --> 01:33:22,730
The future is our world, Morpheus.

1127
01:33:23,070 --> 01:33:25,440
The future is our time.

1128
01:33:29,700 --> 01:33:30,990
There could be a problem.

1129
01:33:31,780 --> 01:33:32,820
What are they doing to him?

1130
01:33:32,820 --> 01:33:35,160
They're breaking into his mind.

1131
01:33:35,410 --> 01:33:37,580
It's like hacking a computer. All it takes is time.

1132
01:33:37,830 --> 01:33:39,040
How much time?

1133
01:33:39,290 --> 01:33:42,420
Depends on the mind. But eventually, it'll crack...

1134
01:33:42,670 --> 01:33:47,090
and his alpha patterns will change from this to this.

1135
01:33:47,340 --> 01:33:50,300
When it does, he'll tell them anything they want to know.

1136
01:33:50,550 --> 01:33:51,600
What do they want?

1137
01:33:51,850 --> 01:33:53,270
The leader of every ship

1138
01:33:53,270 --> 01:33:55,890
is given codes to Zion's mainframe computer.

1139
01:33:56,140 --> 01:33:57,310
If an agent got the codes

1140
01:33:57,310 --> 01:33:59,060
and got into Zion's mainframe...

1141
01:33:59,310 --> 01:34:02,400
they could destroy us. We can't let that happen.

1142
01:34:02,400 --> 01:34:03,060
Trinity.

1143
01:34:03,230 --> 01:34:04,860
Zion's more important than me...

1144
01:34:05,030 --> 01:34:06,240
or you...

1145
01:34:06,400 --> 01:34:07,610
or even Morpheus.

1146
01:34:11,410 --> 01:34:13,080
There has to be something we can do.

1147
01:34:13,490 --> 01:34:15,490
There is. We pull the plug.

1148
01:34:18,580 --> 01:34:20,330
You're going to kill him?

1149
01:34:20,580 --> 01:34:21,750
Kill Morpheus?

1150
01:34:22,380 --> 01:34:24,000
We don't have a choice.

1151
01:34:30,800 --> 01:34:33,720
Never send a human to do a machine's job.

1152
01:34:33,970 --> 01:34:35,720
If indeed the insider has failed...

1153
01:34:35,970 --> 01:34:39,180
they'll sever the connection as soon as possible, unless...

1154
01:34:39,430 --> 01:34:41,140
They're dead. In either case...

1155
01:34:41,400 --> 01:34:43,500
We have no choice. But continue as planned.

1156
01:34:43,500 --> 01:34:44,940
Deploy the sentinels.

1157
01:34:45,190 --> 01:34:46,280
Immediately.

1158
01:34:51,530 --> 01:34:54,200
Morpheus, you were more than a leader to us.

1159
01:34:55,160 --> 01:34:57,370
You were a father.

1160
01:34:58,910 --> 01:35:00,870
We'll miss you always.

1161
01:35:07,630 --> 01:35:08,960
Stop!

1162
01:35:10,170 --> 01:35:11,380
I don't believe this is happening.

1163
01:35:11,630 --> 01:35:13,680
- Neo, this has to be done. - Does it?

1164
01:35:14,470 --> 01:35:15,850
I don't know.

1165
01:35:16,180 --> 01:35:17,720
This can't be just coincidence. It can't be.

1166
01:35:17,930 --> 01:35:20,100
- What are you talking about? - The Oracle.

1167
01:35:20,350 --> 01:35:22,140
She told me this would happen.

1168
01:35:22,560 --> 01:35:26,730
She told me that I would have to make a choice.

1169
01:35:27,190 --> 01:35:28,440
What choice?

1170
01:35:31,400 --> 01:35:33,910
- What are you doing? - I'm going in.

1171
01:35:34,240 --> 01:35:36,580
- No, you're not. - I have to.

1172
01:35:36,780 --> 01:35:39,000
Neo, Morpheus sacrificed himself

1173
01:35:39,000 --> 01:35:40,410
so that we could get you out.

1174
01:35:40,660 --> 01:35:42,580
There is no way that you're going back in.

1175
01:35:43,170 --> 01:35:44,350
Morpheus did what he did

1176
01:35:44,350 --> 01:35:46,420
because he believed I'm something I'm not.

1177
01:35:48,050 --> 01:35:51,300
- What? - I'm not the One, Trinity.

1178
01:35:51,670 --> 01:35:54,640
- The Oracle hit me with that too. - No, you have to be.

1179
01:35:54,890 --> 01:35:57,550
I'm sorry, I'm not. I'm just another guy.

1180
01:35:58,220 --> 01:35:59,470
No, Neo, that's not true.

1181
01:36:00,060 --> 01:36:01,390
It can't be true.

1182
01:36:01,730 --> 01:36:03,850
Why?

1183
01:36:07,110 --> 01:36:09,220
Neo, this is loco. They've got Morpheus

1184
01:36:09,220 --> 01:36:10,440
in a military-controlled building.

1185
01:36:10,690 --> 01:36:12,500
Even if you somehow got inside,

1186
01:36:12,500 --> 01:36:15,070
those are agents holding him. Three of them.

1187
01:36:16,370 --> 01:36:17,850
I want Morpheus back too,

1188
01:36:17,850 --> 01:36:20,290
but what you're talking about is suicide.

1189
01:36:20,540 --> 01:36:23,330
I know that's what it looks like, but it's not.

1190
01:36:23,580 --> 01:36:25,960
I can't explain to you why it's not.

1191
01:36:27,040 --> 01:36:28,550
Morpheus believed something,

1192
01:36:28,550 --> 01:36:30,750
and he was ready to give his life for it.

1193
01:36:31,000 --> 01:36:34,010
I understand that now. That's why I have to go.

1194
01:36:34,260 --> 01:36:36,800
- Why? - Because I believe in something.

1195
01:36:37,010 --> 01:36:38,760
What?

1196
01:36:39,300 --> 01:36:41,010
I believe I can bring him back.

1197
01:36:57,990 --> 01:36:59,910
- What are you doing? - Going with you.

1198
01:37:00,200 --> 01:37:03,200
- No, you're not. - "No"?

1199
01:37:03,370 --> 01:37:05,500
Let me tell you what I believe.

1200
01:37:06,000 --> 01:37:08,380
I believe Morpheus means more to me than he does to you.

1201
01:37:08,710 --> 01:37:10,680
I believe if you are serious about saving him,

1202
01:37:10,680 --> 01:37:13,010
you're going to need my help.

1203
01:37:13,260 --> 01:37:15,300
And since I am the ranking officer on the ship...

1204
01:37:15,550 --> 01:37:18,430
if you don't like it, I believe you can go to hell.

1205
01:37:19,180 --> 01:37:21,600
Because you aren't going anywhere else.

1206
01:37:22,010 --> 01:37:23,560
Tank...

1207
01:37:23,720 --> 01:37:24,890
load us up.

1208
01:37:34,480 --> 01:37:37,780
I'd like to share a revelation that I've had...

1209
01:37:38,200 --> 01:37:39,740
during my time here.

1210
01:37:39,990 --> 01:37:43,990
It came to me when I tried to classify your species...

1211
01:37:44,240 --> 01:37:46,500
and I realized that...

1212
01:37:46,750 --> 01:37:49,040
you're not actually mammals.

1213
01:37:51,250 --> 01:37:53,710
Every mammal on this planet...

1214
01:37:54,050 --> 01:37:57,210
instinctively develops a natural equilibrium

1215
01:37:57,210 --> 01:37:58,970
with the surrounding environment.

1216
01:37:59,220 --> 01:38:01,050
But you humans do not.

1217
01:38:01,600 --> 01:38:05,140
You move to an area and you multiply...

1218
01:38:05,390 --> 01:38:09,900
and multiply until every natural resource is consumed.

1219
01:38:10,230 --> 01:38:12,310
The only way you can survive...

1220
01:38:12,610 --> 01:38:15,570
is to spread to another area.

1221
01:38:20,990 --> 01:38:23,870
There is another organism on this planet...

1222
01:38:24,120 --> 01:38:26,080
that follows the same pattern.

1223
01:38:26,700 --> 01:38:28,370
Do you know what it is?

1224
01:38:28,750 --> 01:38:30,580
A virus.

1225
01:38:31,920 --> 01:38:34,960
Human beings are a disease.

1226
01:38:35,340 --> 01:38:36,880
A cancer of this planet.

1227
01:38:37,130 --> 01:38:39,260
You are a plague.

1228
01:38:39,800 --> 01:38:42,760
And we are the cure.

1229
01:38:43,760 --> 01:38:45,180
Okay, so what do you need?

1230
01:38:45,810 --> 01:38:46,930
Besides a miracle.

1231
01:38:47,520 --> 01:38:48,730
Guns.

1232
01:38:49,430 --> 01:38:50,770
Lots of guns.

1233
01:39:03,620 --> 01:39:06,160
No one has ever done anything like this.

1234
01:39:07,370 --> 01:39:09,290
That's why it's going to work.

1235
01:39:13,380 --> 01:39:15,340
Why isn't the serum working?

1236
01:39:15,920 --> 01:39:18,210
Perhaps we're asking the wrong questions.

1237
01:39:20,300 --> 01:39:21,550
Leave me with him.

1238
01:39:24,140 --> 01:39:25,260
Now.

1239
01:39:36,480 --> 01:39:38,070
Hold on, Morpheus.

1240
01:39:38,320 --> 01:39:41,030
They're coming for you. They're coming.

1241
01:39:43,410 --> 01:39:45,530
Can you hear me, Morpheus?

1242
01:39:45,780 --> 01:39:48,450
I'm going to be honest...

1243
01:39:48,830 --> 01:39:50,040
with you.

1244
01:39:54,420 --> 01:39:55,830
I...

1245
01:39:56,590 --> 01:39:57,840
hate...

1246
01:39:58,090 --> 01:40:00,050
this place...

1247
01:40:00,380 --> 01:40:02,670
this zoo...

1248
01:40:02,930 --> 01:40:04,050
this prison...

1249
01:40:04,300 --> 01:40:07,470
this reality, whatever you want to call it.

1250
01:40:07,720 --> 01:40:10,020
I can't stand it any longer.

1251
01:40:10,770 --> 01:40:12,640
It's the smell.

1252
01:40:14,020 --> 01:40:15,900
If there is such a thing.

1253
01:40:16,230 --> 01:40:19,520
I feel saturated by it.

1254
01:40:21,030 --> 01:40:23,450
I can taste...

1255
01:40:24,280 --> 01:40:26,320
your stink.

1256
01:40:26,570 --> 01:40:27,810
And every time I do,

1257
01:40:27,810 --> 01:40:30,330
I fear that I have somehow been infected by it.

1258
01:40:30,580 --> 01:40:32,200
It's repulsive.

1259
01:40:32,370 --> 01:40:33,750
Isn't it?

1260
01:40:35,920 --> 01:40:38,210
I must get out of here.

1261
01:40:38,630 --> 01:40:40,840
I must get free.

1262
01:40:41,090 --> 01:40:43,970
And in this mind is the key.

1263
01:40:44,220 --> 01:40:45,880
My key.

1264
01:40:46,130 --> 01:40:49,010
Once Zion is destroyed, there is no need for me to be here.

1265
01:40:49,260 --> 01:40:50,890
Do you understand?

1266
01:40:51,180 --> 01:40:52,560
I need the codes.

1267
01:40:52,810 --> 01:40:55,140
I have to get inside Zion...

1268
01:40:55,480 --> 01:40:57,980
and you have to tell me how.

1269
01:40:58,400 --> 01:41:00,270
You're going to tell me...

1270
01:41:00,520 --> 01:41:02,690
or you're going to die.

1271
01:41:22,880 --> 01:41:24,430
Please remove any metallic

1272
01:41:24,430 --> 01:41:26,930
items you're carrying. Keys, loose change.

1273
01:41:29,930 --> 01:41:30,970
Holy shit!

1274
01:41:43,070 --> 01:41:45,780
Backup. Send backup.

1275
01:42:09,550 --> 01:42:10,720
Freeze!

1276
01:44:25,770 --> 01:44:27,900
What were you doing?

1277
01:44:28,610 --> 01:44:29,900
He doesn't know.

1278
01:44:30,150 --> 01:44:31,650
Know what?

1279
01:44:59,720 --> 01:45:02,220
I think they're trying to save him.

1280
01:45:17,070 --> 01:45:18,820
There is no spoon.

1281
01:45:48,440 --> 01:45:50,610
Find them and destroy them!

1282
01:45:52,230 --> 01:45:54,110
I repeat. We're under attack!

1283
01:46:26,040 --> 01:46:28,940
Trinity! Help!

1284
01:46:50,960 --> 01:46:52,170
Only human.

1285
01:46:53,250 --> 01:46:55,130
Dodge this.

1286
01:47:07,430 --> 01:47:08,980
- How did you do that? - Do what?

1287
01:47:09,350 --> 01:47:10,590
You moved like they do.

1288
01:47:10,590 --> 01:47:13,270
I've never seen anyone move that fast.

1289
01:47:14,400 --> 01:47:15,770
It wasn't fast enough.

1290
01:47:18,530 --> 01:47:19,820
Can you fly that thing?

1291
01:47:21,150 --> 01:47:22,950
Not yet.

1292
01:47:25,160 --> 01:47:26,290
Operator.

1293
01:47:26,490 --> 01:47:29,660
Tank, I need a pilot program for a B-212 helicopter.

1294
01:47:30,120 --> 01:47:31,420
Hurry.

1295
01:47:39,340 --> 01:47:40,970
Let's go.

1296
01:47:56,060 --> 01:47:57,150
No.

1297
01:48:48,740 --> 01:48:51,370
Morpheus, get up. Get up, get up.

1298
01:49:29,410 --> 01:49:31,160
He's not going to make it.

1299
01:49:40,250 --> 01:49:41,300
Got you.

1300
01:51:30,200 --> 01:51:31,610
I knew it.

1301
01:51:32,110 --> 01:51:33,450
He's the One.

1302
01:51:49,420 --> 01:51:51,630
Do you believe it now, Trinity?

1303
01:51:54,220 --> 01:51:55,460
Morpheus.

1304
01:51:57,470 --> 01:51:59,520
The Oracle.

1305
01:51:59,680 --> 01:52:02,060
- She told me... - She told you...

1306
01:52:02,440 --> 01:52:04,020
what you needed to hear.

1307
01:52:04,310 --> 01:52:05,650
That's all.

1308
01:52:06,690 --> 01:52:09,650
Neo, Sooner or later you'll realize, just as I did.

1309
01:52:09,990 --> 01:52:12,280
There's a difference between knowing the path...

1310
01:52:13,030 --> 01:52:14,320
and walking the path.

1311
01:52:17,370 --> 01:52:18,580
- Operator. - Tank.

1312
01:52:19,490 --> 01:52:21,310
God damn it. It's good to hear your voice, Sir.

1313
01:52:21,310 --> 01:52:22,040
We need an exit.

1314
01:52:22,290 --> 01:52:23,060
Got one ready.

1315
01:52:23,060 --> 01:52:25,080
Subway station, State and Balboa.

1316
01:52:37,510 --> 01:52:39,100
Damn it!

1317
01:52:39,350 --> 01:52:40,560
The trace was completed.

1318
01:52:40,810 --> 01:52:42,120
We have their position.

1319
01:52:42,120 --> 01:52:44,390
Sentinels are standing by.

1320
01:52:46,100 --> 01:52:47,610
Order the strike.

1321
01:52:54,150 --> 01:52:56,200
They're not out yet.

1322
01:53:07,330 --> 01:53:08,670
You first, Morpheus.

1323
01:53:29,360 --> 01:53:31,650
Neo, I want to tell you something...

1324
01:53:34,900 --> 01:53:38,870
but I'm afraid of what it could mean if I do.

1325
01:53:42,450 --> 01:53:45,750
Everything the Oracle told me has come true.

1326
01:53:48,500 --> 01:53:50,040
Everything but this.

1327
01:53:51,460 --> 01:53:52,590
But what?

1328
01:54:17,000 --> 01:54:18,580
Neo.

1329
01:54:18,910 --> 01:54:20,530
- What the hell just happened? - An agent.

1330
01:54:20,780 --> 01:54:22,740
- You have to send me back. - I can't.

1331
01:54:24,750 --> 01:54:26,750
Mr. Anderson.

1332
01:54:28,920 --> 01:54:30,290
Run, Neo. Run.

1333
01:54:35,590 --> 01:54:37,220
What is he doing?

1334
01:54:37,470 --> 01:54:38,720
He's beginning to believe.

1335
01:55:05,700 --> 01:55:07,080
You're empty.

1336
01:55:07,660 --> 01:55:08,960
So are you.

1337
01:55:42,110 --> 01:55:45,120
I'm going to enjoy watching you die...

1338
01:55:46,240 --> 01:55:47,290
Mr. Anderson.

1339
01:56:28,240 --> 01:56:30,330
Jesus, he's killing him.

1340
01:57:56,500 --> 01:57:58,630
You hear that, Mr. Anderson?

1341
01:57:59,380 --> 01:58:02,380
That is the sound of inevitability.

1342
01:58:04,970 --> 01:58:08,300
It is the sound of your death.

1343
01:58:09,220 --> 01:58:11,560
Goodbye, Mr. Anderson.

1344
01:58:11,810 --> 01:58:13,430
My name...

1345
01:58:16,440 --> 01:58:18,480
is Neo.

1346
01:58:50,720 --> 01:58:51,570
What happened?

1347
01:58:51,570 --> 01:58:52,850
I don't know. I lost him.

1349
01:58:55,430 --> 01:58:56,480
Oh, shit.

1350
01:59:08,860 --> 01:59:10,320
Sentinels.

1351
01:59:11,070 --> 01:59:13,330
- How long? - Five, maybe six minutes.

1352
01:59:15,370 --> 01:59:17,540
Tank, charge the EMP.

1353
01:59:17,790 --> 01:59:19,240
We can't use that until he's out.

1354
01:59:19,240 --> 01:59:20,830
I know, Trinity. Don't worry.

1355
01:59:21,920 --> 01:59:23,090
He's gonna make it.

1356
01:59:23,340 --> 01:59:25,210
Flat or pumps? No, just...

1357
01:59:25,460 --> 01:59:28,340
What the shit? That's my phone!

1358
01:59:28,760 --> 01:59:30,340
That guy took my phone!

1359
01:59:32,720 --> 01:59:36,100
- Got him! He's on the run. - Mr. Wizard,

1360
01:59:36,560 --> 01:59:37,930
get me out of here!

1361
01:59:38,180 --> 01:59:40,060
I got an old exit, Wabash and Lake.

1362
01:59:44,110 --> 01:59:45,770
Oh, shit!

1363
02:00:06,590 --> 02:00:08,590
Help! Need a little help!

1364
02:00:10,220 --> 02:00:11,430
The door.

1365
02:00:27,400 --> 02:00:28,900
The door on your left.

1366
02:00:29,820 --> 02:00:31,070
Your other left!

1367
02:00:37,780 --> 02:00:39,040
The back door.

1368
02:00:59,810 --> 02:01:00,930
Oh, no.

1369
02:01:02,600 --> 02:01:04,100
Here they come.

1370
02:01:32,880 --> 02:01:34,130
He's going to make it.

1371
02:01:44,350 --> 02:01:47,480
The fire escape at the end of the alley, Room 303,

1372
02:02:22,390 --> 02:02:23,680
They're inside.

1373
02:02:25,930 --> 02:02:27,060
Hurry, Neo.

1374
02:03:23,120 --> 02:03:24,410
It can't be.

1375
02:03:32,210 --> 02:03:33,590
Check him.

1376
02:03:37,590 --> 02:03:39,130
He's gone.

1377
02:03:45,850 --> 02:03:48,270
Goodbye, Mr. Anderson.

1378
02:03:58,360 --> 02:04:00,320
I'm not afraid anymore.

1379
02:04:01,950 --> 02:04:03,200
The Oracle told me...

1380
02:04:03,370 --> 02:04:06,190
that I'd fall in love with that man.

1381
02:04:06,190 --> 02:04:08,870
The man that I love would be the One.

1382
02:04:12,000 --> 02:04:13,960
So you see...

1383
02:04:14,670 --> 02:04:16,670
you can't be dead.

1384
02:04:18,260 --> 02:04:20,090
You can't be...

1385
02:04:21,630 --> 02:04:23,800
because I love you.

1386
02:04:25,640 --> 02:04:27,350
You hear me?

1387
02:04:28,470 --> 02:04:30,140
I love you.

1388
02:04:54,080 --> 02:04:55,170
Now, get up.

1389
02:05:03,930 --> 02:05:05,010
No.

1390
02:05:31,500 --> 02:05:32,790
How?

1391
02:05:33,660 --> 02:05:34,710
He is the One.

1394
02:07:59,180 --> 02:08:00,890
I know you're out there,

1397
02:08:01,140 --> 02:08:02,980
I can feel you now,

1400
02:08:05,440 --> 02:08:07,030
you're afraid of us,

1401
02:08:07,360 --> 02:08:09,190
you're afraid of change,

1404
02:08:10,400 --> 02:08:11,910
I don't know the future,

1405
02:08:12,160 --> 02:08:14,740
I didn't come here to tell you how this is going to end,

1406
02:08:14,990 --> 02:08:17,950
I came here to tell you how it's going to begin.

1407
02:08:18,910 --> 02:08:20,500
I'll hang up this phone,

1408
02:08:20,750 --> 02:08:21,990
and then I'll show these people

1409
02:08:21,990 --> 02:08:23,830
what you don't want them to see,

1410
